WEBVTT

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:45.142
<i>The hills are alive</i>

00:02:45.449 --> 00:02:49.818
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:02:50.087 --> 00:02:52.521
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

00:02:52.823 --> 00:02:57.658
<i>For a thousand years</i>

00:02:57.928 --> 00:03:01.091
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

00:03:01.331 --> 00:03:05.859
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:03:06.136 --> 00:03:13.304
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:18.679
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

00:03:18.949 --> 00:03:22.009
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

00:03:22.219 --> 00:03:26.519
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.726
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

00:03:30.994 --> 00:03:34.486
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

00:03:34.731 --> 00:03:38.223
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

00:03:38.502 --> 00:03:42.370
<i>To sing through the night</i>

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:46.405
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

00:03:46.743 --> 00:03:52.375
<i>I go to the hills</i>

00:03:52.582 --> 00:03:58.748
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

00:03:59.022 --> 00:04:02.890
<i>I know I will hear</i>

00:04:03.093 --> 00:04:07.587
<i>What I've heard before</i>

00:04:07.864 --> 00:04:12.597
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:20.607
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:26.843
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:36.015
<i>...once more</i>

00:09:18.074 --> 00:09:23.034
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:23.313 --> 00:09:27.977
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:30.186 --> 00:09:32.245
- Reverend Mother.
- Sister Bernice.

00:09:32.489 --> 00:09:35.117
- I simply cannot find her.
- Maria?

00:09:36.192 --> 00:09:37.489
She's missing again.

00:09:38.428 --> 00:09:40.794
We should've put a cowbell
around her neck.

00:09:41.031 --> 00:09:44.091
Have you tried the barn? You know
how much she adores the animals.

00:09:44.367 --> 00:09:47.097
I have looked everywhere.
In all of the usual places.

00:09:47.303 --> 00:09:49.533
Sister, considering it's Maria...

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:52.433
...I suggest you look in someplace
unusual.

00:09:57.714 --> 00:09:59.011
Well, Reverend Mother...

00:09:59.282 --> 00:10:01.842
...I hope this new infraction ends
whatever doubts...

00:10:02.118 --> 00:10:05.349
...you may still have
about Maria's future here.

00:10:05.555 --> 00:10:09.616
I always try to keep faith
in my doubts, Sister Berthe.

00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:12.726
After all, the wool of a black sheep
is just as warm.

00:10:12.962 --> 00:10:17.296
We are not talking about sheep,
black or white, Sister Margaretta.

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:20.970
Of all the candidates for
the novitiate, Maria is the least...

00:10:21.237 --> 00:10:23.728
Children, children.

00:10:24.207 --> 00:10:28.166
We were speculating about
the qualifications of our postulants.

00:10:28.812 --> 00:10:31.804
The Mistress of Novices
and the Mistress of Postulants...

00:10:32.048 --> 00:10:37.350
...were trying to help me
by expressing opposite points of view.

00:10:37.587 --> 00:10:40.647
Tell me, Sister Catherine,
what do you think of Maria?

00:10:40.857 --> 00:10:43.917
She's a wonderful girl,
some of the time.

00:10:44.894 --> 00:10:47.988
- Sister Agatha?
- It's very easy to like Maria...

00:10:48.231 --> 00:10:50.756
...except when it's difficult.

00:10:51.067 --> 00:10:54.628
- And you, Sister Sophia?
- Oh, I love her very dearly.

00:10:54.838 --> 00:10:57.773
But she always seems to be
in trouble, doesn't she?

00:10:58.007 --> 00:10:59.599
Exactly what I say.

00:11:00.076 --> 00:11:02.544
<i>She climbs a tree and scrapes her knee</i>

00:11:02.746 --> 00:11:04.441
<i>Her dress has got a tear</i>

00:11:05.115 --> 00:11:09.279
<i>She waltzes on her way to Mass</i>
<i>And whistles on the stair</i>

00:11:09.919 --> 00:11:14.413
<i>And underneath her wimple</i>
<i>She has curlers in her hair</i>

00:11:14.691 --> 00:11:19.287
<i>I've even heard her singing</i>
<i>In the abbey</i>

00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:21.520
<i>She's always late for chapel</i>

00:11:21.765 --> 00:11:24.029
<i>But her penitence is real</i>

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.632
<i>She's always late for everything</i>

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.895
<i>Except for every meal</i>

00:11:29.272 --> 00:11:33.971
<i>I hate to have to say it</i>
<i>But I very firmly feel</i>

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.647
<i>Maria's not an asset to the abbey</i>

00:11:39.149 --> 00:11:41.640
<i>I'd like to say a word in her behalf</i>

00:11:41.918 --> 00:11:43.249
Say it, Sister Margaretta.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:48.079
<i>Maria makes me laugh</i>

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.896
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:11:55.165 --> 00:11:58.965
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:11:59.269 --> 00:12:02.602
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:04.231
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

00:12:04.474 --> 00:12:05.805
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>- A clown</i>

00:12:07.443 --> 00:12:11.174
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:12:11.447 --> 00:12:14.905
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:12:15.318 --> 00:12:19.015
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

00:12:19.589 --> 00:12:23.081
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:12:23.326 --> 00:12:27.422
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:12:27.931 --> 00:12:33.460
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:39.131
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.702
<i>When I'm with her I'm confused</i>
<i>Out of focus and bemused</i>

00:12:44.013 --> 00:12:47.449
<i>And I never know exactly where I am</i>

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:50.983
<i>- Unpredictable as weather</i>
<i>- She's as flighty as a feather</i>

00:12:51.354 --> 00:12:53.185
<i>- She's a darling</i>
<i>- She's a demon</i>

00:12:53.389 --> 00:12:54.720
<i>She's a lamb</i>

00:12:55.124 --> 00:12:58.787
<i>She'll out pester any pest</i>
<i>Drive a hornet from its nest</i>

00:12:58.995 --> 00:13:02.294
<i>She can throw a whirling dervish</i>
<i>Out of whirl</i>

00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:06.393
<i>- She is gentle, she is wild</i>
<i>- She's a riddle, she's a child</i>

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.530
<i>- She's a headache</i>
<i>- She's an angel</i>

00:13:09.739 --> 00:13:13.641
<i>She's a girl</i>

00:13:14.377 --> 00:13:18.313
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:13:18.548 --> 00:13:22.245
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:13:22.552 --> 00:13:26.044
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:13:26.322 --> 00:13:28.313
<i>- A flibbertigibbet</i>
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>

00:13:28.558 --> 00:13:30.185
<i>A clown</i>

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.391
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:13:34.664 --> 00:13:38.156
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:13:38.368 --> 00:13:42.702
<i>- But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>- And listen to all you say?</i>

00:13:42.939 --> 00:13:47.035
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:13:47.243 --> 00:13:53.079
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:14:09.032 --> 00:14:15.801
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:14:16.706 --> 00:14:23.111
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:14:34.924 --> 00:14:36.915
You may go in now, Maria.

00:14:49.505 --> 00:14:51.132
Come here, my child.

00:14:57.647 --> 00:14:59.012
Now sit down.

00:14:59.949 --> 00:15:03.510
Reverend Mother, I'm sorry.
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:03.786 --> 00:15:06.755
- The hills were beckoning and before...
- Dear.

00:15:07.156 --> 00:15:09.124
I haven't summoned you for apologies.

00:15:09.359 --> 00:15:11.589
Please let me ask for forgiveness.

00:15:12.261 --> 00:15:13.489
If you'll feel better.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.796
Yes, you see,
the sky was so blue today...

00:15:17.033 --> 00:15:20.833
...and everything was so green and
fragrant, I had to be a part of it.

00:15:21.104 --> 00:15:25.598
The Untersberg led me higher like
it wanted me to go through the clouds.

00:15:25.808 --> 00:15:27.833
Suppose darkness had come
and you were lost?

00:15:28.111 --> 00:15:30.341
Mother, I could never be lost
up there.

00:15:30.613 --> 00:15:33.446
That's my mountain.
I was brought up on it.

00:15:33.649 --> 00:15:35.947
It was the mountain that led me
to you.

00:15:36.719 --> 00:15:39.688
When I was a child,
I would come down and climb a tree...

00:15:39.956 --> 00:15:41.719
...and look in your garden.

00:15:41.958 --> 00:15:44.893
I'd see the sisters at work
and hear them sing.

00:15:46.229 --> 00:15:49.858
Which brings me to another
transgression, Reverend Mother.

00:15:50.066 --> 00:15:52.227
I was singing out there today.

00:15:52.902 --> 00:15:56.929
Only in the abbey do we have rules
about postulants singing.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.165
I can't stop wherever I am.

00:15:59.375 --> 00:16:01.707
Worse, I can't seem to stop
saying things.

00:16:01.978 --> 00:16:04.242
Everything I think and feel.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.913
Some call that "honesty."

00:16:06.182 --> 00:16:08.548
Oh, but it's terrible,
Reverend Mother!

00:16:08.751 --> 00:16:12.653
You know how Sister Berthe makes me
kiss the floor after a disagreement?

00:16:13.022 --> 00:16:16.514
Lately, I kiss the floor
when I see her coming to save time.

00:16:19.195 --> 00:16:20.355
Maria...

00:16:21.364 --> 00:16:24.356
...when you saw us over the wall
and longed to be with us...

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:29.333
...that didn't mean you were prepared
for the way we live here, did it?

00:16:30.673 --> 00:16:33.073
No, Mother, but I pray and I try.

00:16:33.276 --> 00:16:35.005
And I am learning. I really am.

00:16:35.244 --> 00:16:37.906
What is the most important lesson
you have learned here?

00:16:38.581 --> 00:16:42.381
To find out what is the will of God
and do it wholeheartedly.

00:16:45.221 --> 00:16:46.347
Maria...

00:16:47.857 --> 00:16:50.621
...it seems to be God's will
that you leave us.

00:16:50.893 --> 00:16:52.383
- Leave?
- Only for a while.

00:16:52.895 --> 00:16:55.227
No, Mother!
Please don't send me away!

00:16:55.465 --> 00:16:59.731
This is where I belong. It's my home,
my family. It's my life.

00:17:00.403 --> 00:17:03.429
- Are you truly ready for it?
- Yes, I am.

00:17:03.639 --> 00:17:08.542
If you go out into the world for a
time, knowing what we expect of you...

00:17:08.811 --> 00:17:11.541
...you will find out
if you can expect it of yourself.

00:17:11.747 --> 00:17:16.047
I know what you expect, Mother,
and I can do it! I promise I can!

00:17:19.589 --> 00:17:20.817
Yes, Mother.

00:17:22.925 --> 00:17:24.586
If it is God's will.

00:17:26.829 --> 00:17:31.960
There is a family near Salzburg that
needs a governess until September.

00:17:32.168 --> 00:17:34.398
- September?
- For seven children.

00:17:35.071 --> 00:17:36.060
Seven children?!

00:17:36.305 --> 00:17:37.567
Do you like children?

00:17:38.341 --> 00:17:40.172
Well, yes, but seven!

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:44.473
I will tell Captain von Trapp
to expect you tomorrow.

00:17:45.014 --> 00:17:46.413
Captain?

00:17:47.116 --> 00:17:51.951
A retired officer of the Imperial
Navy. A fine man and a brave one.

00:17:52.188 --> 00:17:54.918
His wife died,
and he is alone with the children.

00:17:55.124 --> 00:17:59.424
I understand he has had a difficult
time keeping a governess there.

00:18:00.196 --> 00:18:02.494
Why difficult, Reverend Mother?

00:18:03.866 --> 00:18:06.801
The Lord will show you
in His own good time.

00:18:43.673 --> 00:18:46.141
When the Lord closes a door...

00:18:46.342 --> 00:18:48.867
...somewhere He opens a window.

00:18:51.214 --> 00:18:56.208
<i>What will this day be like?</i>

00:18:56.419 --> 00:18:58.649
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:05.161 --> 00:19:09.257
<i>What will my future be?</i>

00:19:10.099 --> 00:19:12.363
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:13.936 --> 00:19:17.030
<i>It could be so exciting</i>

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:20.334
<i>To be out in the world</i>
<i>To be free</i>

00:19:20.543 --> 00:19:23.603
<i>My heart should be wildly rejoicing</i>

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:30.116
<i>Oh, what's the matter with me?</i>

00:19:30.453 --> 00:19:33.513
<i>I've always longed for adventure</i>

00:19:33.789 --> 00:19:37.350
<i>To do the things I've never dared</i>

00:19:37.593 --> 00:19:40.790
<i>Now here I'm facing adventure</i>

00:19:41.097 --> 00:19:47.195
<i>Then why am I so scared?</i>

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.541
<i>A captain with seven children</i>

00:19:53.776 --> 00:19:56.609
<i>What's so fearsome about that?</i>

00:19:59.148 --> 00:20:01.776
<i>I must stop these doubts and worries</i>

00:20:02.051 --> 00:20:04.884
<i>If I don't I just know I'll turn back</i>

00:20:05.154 --> 00:20:08.317
<i>I must dream of the things</i>
<i>I am seeking</i>

00:20:09.392 --> 00:20:14.386
<i>I am seeking the courage I lack</i>

00:20:15.298 --> 00:20:19.132
<i>The courage to serve them</i>
<i>With reliance</i>

00:20:19.402 --> 00:20:22.303
<i>Face my mistakes without defiance</i>

00:20:22.571 --> 00:20:24.266
<i>Show them I'm worthy</i>

00:20:24.507 --> 00:20:27.169
<i>And while I show them</i>

00:20:27.443 --> 00:20:31.243
<i>I'll show me</i>

00:20:31.447 --> 00:20:36.851
<i>So let them bring on</i>
<i>All their problems</i>

00:20:37.086 --> 00:20:40.351
<i>I'll do better than my best</i>

00:20:40.623 --> 00:20:43.683
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>They'll put me to the test</i>

00:20:43.926 --> 00:20:47.362
<i>But I'll make them see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:20:47.596 --> 00:20:50.861
<i>Somehow I will impress them</i>

00:20:51.133 --> 00:20:54.364
<i>I will be firm but kind</i>

00:20:54.637 --> 00:20:57.936
<i>And all those children</i>
<i>Heaven bless them</i>

00:20:58.174 --> 00:21:01.473
<i>They will look up to me</i>
<i>And mind me</i>

00:21:01.711 --> 00:21:04.839
<i>With each step I am more certain</i>

00:21:05.114 --> 00:21:08.379
<i>Everything will turn out fine</i>

00:21:08.617 --> 00:21:11.711
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>The world can all be mine</i>

00:21:11.954 --> 00:21:17.392
<i>They'll have to agree</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:18.961 --> 00:21:21.691
<i>I have confidence in sunshine</i>

00:21:21.964 --> 00:21:25.058
<i>I have confidence in rain</i>

00:21:25.301 --> 00:21:28.168
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>That spring will come again</i>

00:21:28.471 --> 00:21:31.497
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:31.807 --> 00:21:34.867
<i>Strength doesn't lie in numbers</i>

00:21:35.144 --> 00:21:38.170
<i>Strength doesn't lie in wealth</i>

00:21:38.414 --> 00:21:41.747
<i>Strength lies in nights</i>
<i>Of peaceful slumbers</i>

00:21:42.017 --> 00:21:44.884
<i>When you wake up, wake up</i>
<i>It's healthy</i>

00:21:45.187 --> 00:21:48.179
<i>All I trust I leave my heart to</i>

00:21:48.424 --> 00:21:51.325
<i>All I trust becomes my own</i>

00:21:51.527 --> 00:21:56.328
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:10.946 --> 00:22:12.573
Oh, help.

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:31.427
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:32.234 --> 00:22:37.035
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence...</i>

00:22:37.306 --> 00:22:44.109
<i>...in me</i>

00:22:50.653 --> 00:22:53.053
Hello. Here I am.

00:22:55.891 --> 00:22:57.722
I'm from the convent.
I'm the new governess, captain.

00:22:59.395 --> 00:23:02.626
And I'm the old butler, fräulein.

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:06.397
Well, how do you do?

00:23:16.912 --> 00:23:20.973
You'll wait here, please.

00:24:47.336 --> 00:24:51.432
In future, remember certain rooms
in this house are not to be disturbed.

00:24:52.608 --> 00:24:54.075
Yes, captain, sir.

00:25:02.017 --> 00:25:07.250
- Why do you stare at me that way?
- You don't look like a sea captain.

00:25:08.457 --> 00:25:11.517
I'm afraid you don't look
very much like a governess.

00:25:12.227 --> 00:25:13.285
- Turn around.
- What?

00:25:13.629 --> 00:25:14.891
Turn.

00:25:18.067 --> 00:25:19.227
Hat off.

00:25:22.438 --> 00:25:25.066
Put on another dress
before meeting the children.

00:25:25.374 --> 00:25:26.932
But I don't have another.

00:25:27.209 --> 00:25:30.076
When we enter the abbey,
our worldly clothes go to the poor.

00:25:30.312 --> 00:25:31.574
What about this one?

00:25:31.780 --> 00:25:33.111
The poor didn't want it.

00:25:34.950 --> 00:25:38.442
There wasn't time to make a new dress.
I can make clothes.

00:25:39.722 --> 00:25:41.986
I'll see that you get some material.

00:25:42.725 --> 00:25:44.249
Today, if possible.

00:25:45.227 --> 00:25:46.990
- Now, fräulein...
- Maria.

00:25:47.229 --> 00:25:49.959
I don't know how much
the abbess told you.

00:25:50.232 --> 00:25:52.792
You are the twelfth governess...

00:25:53.002 --> 00:25:55.470
...to look after my children
since their mother died.

00:25:55.671 --> 00:25:57.901
I trust you will be an improvement
on the last one.

00:25:58.140 --> 00:25:59.971
She stayed only two hours.

00:26:01.677 --> 00:26:04.271
What's wrong with the children, sir?

00:26:05.748 --> 00:26:10.151
Nothing is wrong with the children,
only the governesses.

00:26:10.419 --> 00:26:15.356
They could not maintain discipline,
without which the house cannot be run.

00:26:16.291 --> 00:26:18.088
Drill them in their studies.

00:26:18.327 --> 00:26:21.819
I will not permit them to dream
away their summer holidays.

00:26:22.097 --> 00:26:24.793
Each afternoon,
they march, breathing deeply.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:26.661
Bedtime is to be strictly observed.

00:26:26.869 --> 00:26:27.836
When do they play?

00:26:28.037 --> 00:26:32.098
You will see to it that they conduct
themselves with the utmost decorum.

00:26:32.341 --> 00:26:35.276
- I am placing you in command.
- Yes, sir.

00:27:55.924 --> 00:27:57.084
Now...

00:27:57.693 --> 00:28:00.628
...this is your new governess,
Fräulein Maria.

00:28:02.297 --> 00:28:04.288
Give your name at your signal.

00:28:04.600 --> 00:28:08.798
Fräulein, listen carefully. Learn
their signals so you can call them.

00:28:10.105 --> 00:28:11.470
Liesl.

00:28:11.740 --> 00:28:13.469
Friedrich.

00:28:13.742 --> 00:28:15.266
Louisa.

00:28:15.544 --> 00:28:16.806
Kurt.

00:28:17.045 --> 00:28:18.103
Brigitta.

00:28:18.380 --> 00:28:19.608
Marta.

00:28:25.988 --> 00:28:27.319
Gretl.

00:28:31.960 --> 00:28:35.396
Now, let's see how well you listened.

00:28:35.631 --> 00:28:37.997
I won't need to whistle for them,
Reverend Captain.

00:28:38.267 --> 00:28:41.725
I mean, I'll use their names.
Such lovely names.

00:28:41.937 --> 00:28:45.100
Fräulein, this is a large house.
The grounds are extensive.

00:28:45.340 --> 00:28:48.104
And I will not have anyone shouting.

00:28:48.343 --> 00:28:50.072
You will take this, please.
Learn to use it.

00:28:50.279 --> 00:28:51.940
The children will help you.

00:28:53.982 --> 00:28:57.975
Now, when I want you,
this is what you will hear.

00:28:58.854 --> 00:29:00.651
Oh, no, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:29:01.523 --> 00:29:03.081
I could never answer to a whistle.

00:29:03.292 --> 00:29:05.920
Whistles are for animals,
not for children.

00:29:06.195 --> 00:29:08.254
And definitely not for me.

00:29:08.497 --> 00:29:11.125
It would be too humiliating.

00:29:11.934 --> 00:29:17.133
Fräulein, were you this much trouble
at the abbey?

00:29:17.439 --> 00:29:18.531
Oh, much more, sir.

00:29:29.651 --> 00:29:31.209
I don't know your signal.

00:29:32.688 --> 00:29:35.316
You may call me "captain."

00:29:48.237 --> 00:29:49.704
At ease.

00:29:52.507 --> 00:29:54.065
Now that there's just us...

00:29:54.343 --> 00:29:58.507
...would you please tell me all your
names again and how old you are.

00:29:58.981 --> 00:30:02.974
I'm Liesl. I'm 16 years old,
and I don't need a governess.

00:30:03.752 --> 00:30:06.812
I'm glad you told me, Liesl.
We'll just be good friends.

00:30:08.991 --> 00:30:12.757
I'm Friedrich. I'm 14.
I'm impossible.

00:30:13.061 --> 00:30:14.722
Really? Who told you that, Friedrich?

00:30:14.997 --> 00:30:18.489
Fräulein Josephine.
Four governesses ago.

00:30:18.934 --> 00:30:20.401
I'm Brigitta.

00:30:22.237 --> 00:30:26.230
You didn't tell me how old you are,
Louisa.

00:30:26.909 --> 00:30:29.173
I'm Brigitta. She's Louisa.

00:30:29.411 --> 00:30:32.175
She's 13 years old, and you're smart.

00:30:32.414 --> 00:30:36.180
I'm 10, and I think your dress
is the ugliest one I ever saw.

00:30:36.518 --> 00:30:39.146
- Brigitta, you shouldn't say that.
- Why not?

00:30:39.354 --> 00:30:41.618
- Don't you think it's ugly?
- Of course.

00:30:41.890 --> 00:30:44.586
But Fräulein Helga's was ugliest.

00:30:44.860 --> 00:30:47.454
I'm Kurt. I'm 11.
I'm incorrigible.

00:30:47.729 --> 00:30:50.857
- Congratulations.
- What's "incorrigible"?

00:30:51.099 --> 00:30:54.967
I think it means you want
to be treated like a boy.

00:30:57.139 --> 00:31:00.438
I'm Marta, and I'm going to be
seven on Tuesday.

00:31:00.709 --> 00:31:02.074
I'd like a pink parasol.

00:31:03.278 --> 00:31:04.802
Pink's my favorite color too.

00:31:07.215 --> 00:31:08.375
Yes, you're Gretl.

00:31:09.284 --> 00:31:10.979
And you're five years old?

00:31:11.420 --> 00:31:13.411
My, you're practically a lady.

00:31:15.924 --> 00:31:18.950
I have to tell you a secret.
I've never been a governess.

00:31:20.395 --> 00:31:23.159
You don't know anything
about being a governess?

00:31:23.432 --> 00:31:24.797
Nothing. I'll need lots of advice.

00:31:25.767 --> 00:31:30.295
The best way to start is to tell
Father to mind his own business.

00:31:30.505 --> 00:31:32.302
Never come to dinner on time.

00:31:32.507 --> 00:31:34.805
Never eat your soup quietly.

00:31:35.477 --> 00:31:37.570
During dessert, always blow your nose.

00:31:37.813 --> 00:31:40.611
Don't you believe a word they say,
Fräulein Maria.

00:31:40.816 --> 00:31:44.183
- Oh, why not?
- Because I like you.

00:31:44.987 --> 00:31:46.978
Children, outside for your walk.

00:31:47.189 --> 00:31:49.089
Father's orders. Hurry up.

00:31:49.291 --> 00:31:50.588
Quick, quick, quick.

00:31:50.826 --> 00:31:54.023
Fräulein Maria, I'm Frau Schmidt,
the housekeeper.

00:31:54.262 --> 00:31:55.320
How do you do.

00:31:55.530 --> 00:31:58.431
I'll show you to your room.
Follow me.

00:32:09.511 --> 00:32:11.274
Poor little dears.

00:32:23.992 --> 00:32:28.361
You're very lucky. With
Fräulein Helga it was a snake.

00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:43.541
Good evening.

00:32:44.980 --> 00:32:48.541
- Good evening, children.
- Good evening, Fräulein Maria.

00:32:55.757 --> 00:32:57.384
Enchanting little ritual.

00:32:57.592 --> 00:33:00.322
Something you learned at the abbey?

00:33:01.530 --> 00:33:03.862
No.

00:33:05.500 --> 00:33:06.762
Rheumatism.

00:33:16.578 --> 00:33:19.741
Excuse me, captain. Haven't we
forgotten to thank the Lord?

00:33:27.956 --> 00:33:30.925
For what we receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

00:33:31.460 --> 00:33:33.394
- Amen.
- Amen.

00:33:37.933 --> 00:33:39.867
I'd like to thank you all...

00:33:40.068 --> 00:33:43.060
...for the precious gift
you left in my pocket today.

00:33:46.575 --> 00:33:48.372
What gift?

00:33:51.480 --> 00:33:53.641
It's a secret between
the children and me.

00:33:53.915 --> 00:33:57.544
Then I suggest you keep it,
and let us eat.

00:33:57.919 --> 00:33:59.887
Knowing how nervous
I must have been...

00:34:00.122 --> 00:34:02.556
...a stranger in a new household...

00:34:02.757 --> 00:34:05.817
...knowing how important it was
for me to feel accepted...

00:34:06.094 --> 00:34:10.292
...it was so kind and thoughtful of
you to make my first moments here...

00:34:10.565 --> 00:34:12.760
...so warm and happy...

00:34:12.968 --> 00:34:14.731
...and pleasant.

00:34:23.979 --> 00:34:26.004
- What is the matter, Marta?
- Nothing.

00:34:38.426 --> 00:34:39.450
Fräulein...

00:34:39.694 --> 00:34:43.528
...is it to be at every meal
or merely at dinnertime...

00:34:43.765 --> 00:34:48.327
...that you intend leading us through
this rare and wonderful new world...

00:34:48.537 --> 00:34:50.198
...of indigestion?

00:34:51.773 --> 00:34:54.640
They're all right, captain.
They're just happy.

00:35:13.395 --> 00:35:16.057
- Rolfe, good evening.
- Good evening, Franz.

00:35:16.331 --> 00:35:19.061
- I trust everything is under control?
- Yes, yes.

00:35:20.702 --> 00:35:23.136
- Are there any developments?
- Perhaps.

00:35:23.338 --> 00:35:25.499
- Is the captain home?
- He's at dinner.

00:35:25.740 --> 00:35:28.072
- With the family?
- Yes.

00:35:28.343 --> 00:35:30.140
Give him this telegram at once.

00:35:30.879 --> 00:35:31.971
Certainly.

00:35:43.658 --> 00:35:45.353
A telegram for you, sir.

00:35:48.196 --> 00:35:50.027
Franz? Who delivered it?

00:35:50.332 --> 00:35:52.357
That young lad Rolfe, of course.

00:35:54.703 --> 00:35:56.432
Father, may I be excused?

00:35:57.405 --> 00:36:01.865
Children, in the morning I shall
be going to Vienna.

00:36:02.177 --> 00:36:04.611
Not again, Father!

00:36:08.516 --> 00:36:10.575
How long will you be gone this time?

00:36:11.219 --> 00:36:12.686
I'm not sure, Gretl.

00:36:12.887 --> 00:36:16.448
- To visit Baroness Schraeder again?
- Mind your own business!

00:36:17.425 --> 00:36:19.359
As a matter of fact, yes, Louisa.

00:36:21.129 --> 00:36:24.963
- Why can't we ever see the baroness?
- Why would she want to see you?

00:36:25.267 --> 00:36:30.136
You are going to see the baroness.
I'm bringing her back with me to visit.

00:36:31.640 --> 00:36:33.437
And Uncle Max.

00:36:33.708 --> 00:36:36.108
Uncle Max!

00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:53.491
Rolfe!

00:36:56.564 --> 00:36:57.622
Oh, Rolfe!

00:37:00.168 --> 00:37:03.103
- No, Liesl. We mustn't!
- Why not, silly?

00:37:03.338 --> 00:37:06.000
- I don't know...
- Isn't this why you're waiting?

00:37:06.241 --> 00:37:08.106
Yes, of course.

00:37:08.310 --> 00:37:11.108
- I've missed you, Liesl.
- You have? How much?

00:37:11.346 --> 00:37:15.180
I even thought of sending a telegram,
so I'd be able to deliver it here.

00:37:15.450 --> 00:37:19.352
Oh, that's a lovely thought!
Why don't you, right now?

00:37:19.621 --> 00:37:23.785
- But I'm here!
- Please, Rolfe. Send me a telegram.

00:37:23.992 --> 00:37:27.450
I'll start it for you.
"Dear Liesl..."

00:37:28.129 --> 00:37:31.758
"Dear Liesl: I'd like to be able
to tell you...

00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:34.195
...how I feel about you. Stop.

00:37:34.436 --> 00:37:38.964
Unfortunately, this wire
is already too expensive.

00:37:39.174 --> 00:37:40.607
Sincerely, Rolfe."

00:37:40.809 --> 00:37:43.573
- "Sincerely"?
- Cordially.

00:37:43.778 --> 00:37:46.440
- "Cordially"?
- Affectionately?

00:37:48.817 --> 00:37:50.842
Will there be any reply?

00:37:52.120 --> 00:37:54.281
"Dear Rolfe: Stop.

00:37:55.290 --> 00:37:58.384
Don't stop! Your Liesl."

00:38:00.128 --> 00:38:03.962
If only we didn't have to wait
for someone to send Father a telegram.

00:38:04.232 --> 00:38:06.632
How do I know when I'll see you again?

00:38:07.535 --> 00:38:08.729
Well, let's see...

00:38:11.740 --> 00:38:13.708
I could come here by mistake.

00:38:14.709 --> 00:38:19.339
With a telegram for Colonel Schneider!
He's here from Berlin staying with...

00:38:20.248 --> 00:38:23.547
No one knows he's here.
Don't tell your father.

00:38:23.818 --> 00:38:26.981
- Why not?
- Your father's so Austrian.

00:38:27.188 --> 00:38:28.485
We're all Austrian.

00:38:28.690 --> 00:38:33.093
Some think we ought to be German, and
they're very mad at those who don't.

00:38:33.328 --> 00:38:35.091
They're getting ready to...

00:38:36.765 --> 00:38:39.199
Let's hope your father
doesn't get into trouble.

00:38:39.501 --> 00:38:44.404
Don't worry. He's a big naval hero.
He was even decorated by the emperor.

00:38:44.606 --> 00:38:47.871
I don't worry about him.
I worry about his daughter.

00:38:48.410 --> 00:38:49.877
Me? Why?

00:38:50.178 --> 00:38:51.736
- Well, you're so...
- What?

00:38:52.180 --> 00:38:53.670
You're such a baby!

00:38:54.115 --> 00:38:57.016
I'm 16.
What's such a baby about that?

00:38:59.254 --> 00:39:02.781
<i>You wait, little girl</i>
<i>On an empty stage</i>

00:39:03.024 --> 00:39:06.391
<i>For fate to turn the light on</i>

00:39:07.028 --> 00:39:10.259
<i>Your life, little girl</i>
<i>Is an empty page</i>

00:39:10.532 --> 00:39:14.593
<i>That men will want to write on</i>

00:39:15.303 --> 00:39:20.798
<i>To write on</i>

00:39:21.743 --> 00:39:25.679
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:25.880 --> 00:39:29.714
<i>Baby, it's time to think</i>

00:39:29.918 --> 00:39:33.547
<i>Better beware</i>
<i>Be canny and careful</i>

00:39:33.788 --> 00:39:37.417
<i>Baby, you're on the brink</i>

00:39:37.759 --> 00:39:41.593
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:41.796 --> 00:39:45.459
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

00:39:45.767 --> 00:39:49.100
<i>Eager young lads</i>
<i>And roués and cads</i>

00:39:49.304 --> 00:39:53.240
<i>Will offer you food and wine</i>

00:39:53.508 --> 00:39:57.274
<i>Totally unprepared are you</i>

00:39:57.679 --> 00:40:01.240
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:40:01.816 --> 00:40:05.980
<i>Timid and shy and scared are you</i>

00:40:06.287 --> 00:40:09.779
<i>Of things beyond your ken</i>

00:40:09.991 --> 00:40:13.859
<i>You need someone older and wiser</i>

00:40:14.095 --> 00:40:17.963
<i>Telling you what to do</i>

00:40:18.199 --> 00:40:21.635
<i>I am 17 going on 18</i>

00:40:21.870 --> 00:40:27.831
<i>I'll take care of you</i>

00:41:00.375 --> 00:41:03.708
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:03.912 --> 00:41:07.313
<i>I know that I'm naive</i>

00:41:07.582 --> 00:41:10.813
<i>Fellows I meet</i>
<i>May tell me I'm sweet</i>

00:41:11.052 --> 00:41:14.749
<i>And willingly I believe</i>

00:41:15.223 --> 00:41:18.386
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:18.593 --> 00:41:22.359
<i>Innocent as a rose</i>

00:41:22.564 --> 00:41:26.022
<i>Bachelor dandies</i>
<i>Drinkers of brandies</i>

00:41:26.334 --> 00:41:29.667
<i>What do I know of those?</i>

00:41:29.871 --> 00:41:33.398
<i>Totally unprepared am I</i>

00:41:33.675 --> 00:41:37.167
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:41:37.579 --> 00:41:40.912
<i>Timid and shy and scared am I</i>

00:41:41.182 --> 00:41:44.845
<i>Of things beyond my ken</i>

00:41:45.286 --> 00:41:48.881
<i>I need someone older and wiser</i>

00:41:49.123 --> 00:41:52.422
<i>Telling me what to do</i>

00:41:52.760 --> 00:41:56.457
<i>You are 17 going on 18</i>

00:41:56.698 --> 00:42:02.364
<i>I'll depend on you</i>

00:43:55.416 --> 00:43:56.849
Come in.

00:43:57.885 --> 00:43:59.512
Frau Schmidt.

00:44:01.856 --> 00:44:03.585
For your new dresses.

00:44:03.891 --> 00:44:07.884
- The captain had these sent from town.
- Oh, how lovely!

00:44:08.162 --> 00:44:11.598
These will make the prettiest
clothes I've ever had.

00:44:11.866 --> 00:44:15.358
Do you think he would
get me more material if I asked?

00:44:15.603 --> 00:44:19.232
- How many dresses do you need?
- Not for me, for the children.

00:44:19.507 --> 00:44:21.566
I want to make them some play clothes.

00:44:21.843 --> 00:44:25.370
The von Trapp children don't play.
They march.

00:44:25.880 --> 00:44:28.280
Surely you don't approve of that.

00:44:29.283 --> 00:44:31.683
Ever since the captain
lost his poor wife...

00:44:31.919 --> 00:44:34.615
...he runs this house as if on
one of his ships.

00:44:35.456 --> 00:44:36.855
Whistles, orders.

00:44:37.125 --> 00:44:38.956
No more music, no more laughing.

00:44:39.227 --> 00:44:42.754
Nothing that reminds him of her.
Even the children.

00:44:43.264 --> 00:44:44.356
But that's so wrong.

00:44:45.199 --> 00:44:46.723
Oh, well.

00:44:46.934 --> 00:44:50.597
How do you like your room?
There'll be new drapes at the windows.

00:44:50.872 --> 00:44:52.134
Bu these are fine.

00:44:52.373 --> 00:44:54.034
New ones have been ordered.

00:44:54.242 --> 00:44:57.541
- But I really don't need them.
- Good night, now.

00:44:57.779 --> 00:45:01.806
Frau Schmidt, if I asked
the captain about the material...?

00:45:02.083 --> 00:45:06.543
- He's leaving in the morning.
- Of course. How long will he be gone?

00:45:07.121 --> 00:45:11.717
It depends. The last time he visited
the baroness, he stayed for a month.

00:45:12.894 --> 00:45:17.456
I shouldn't be saying this to you.
I don't know you that well.

00:45:17.732 --> 00:45:20.633
But if you ask me,
the captain's thinking seriously...

00:45:20.835 --> 00:45:23.133
...of marrying her before
summer's over.

00:45:23.337 --> 00:45:26.568
Wonderful! The children will
have a mother again.

00:45:28.009 --> 00:45:29.306
Yes.

00:45:29.577 --> 00:45:31.306
Well, good night.

00:45:31.512 --> 00:45:32.945
Good night.

00:45:51.365 --> 00:45:54.198
Dear Father, now I know
why You sent me here.

00:45:54.435 --> 00:45:57.302
To help these children
prepare for a new mother.

00:45:57.538 --> 00:46:00.837
And I pray this will become
a happy family in Thy sight.

00:46:01.042 --> 00:46:04.170
God bless the captain.
God bless Liesl and Friedrich.

00:46:04.378 --> 00:46:08.542
God bless Louisa, Brigitta,
Marta and little Gretl.

00:46:08.850 --> 00:46:11.683
And I forgot the other boy.
What's his name?

00:46:13.454 --> 00:46:15.285
Well, God bless what's-his-name.

00:46:15.489 --> 00:46:19.482
God bless the Reverend Mother
and Sister Margaretta...

00:46:19.694 --> 00:46:21.491
...and everybody at the abbey.

00:46:21.696 --> 00:46:24.221
And now, dear God, about Liesl.

00:46:24.732 --> 00:46:26.632
Help her know that I'm her friend...

00:46:26.834 --> 00:46:29.394
...and help her tell me
what she's been up to.

00:46:30.137 --> 00:46:31.297
Are you going to tell on me?

00:46:31.539 --> 00:46:34.975
Help me to be understanding
so I may guide her footsteps.

00:46:35.243 --> 00:46:37.871
In the name of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost.

00:46:38.079 --> 00:46:41.071
I was out walking
and somebody locked the doors early.

00:46:41.382 --> 00:46:45.011
I didn't want to wake everybody,
so when I saw your window open...

00:46:46.654 --> 00:46:49.680
You're not going to tell Father,
are you?

00:46:55.763 --> 00:46:57.060
How did you climb up?

00:46:57.565 --> 00:47:00.693
It's how we always got in
to play tricks on the governess.

00:47:00.902 --> 00:47:03.894
Louisa can make it with
a whole jar of spiders in her hand.

00:47:04.906 --> 00:47:06.567
Spiders?

00:47:10.278 --> 00:47:12.906
Were you out walking all by yourself?

00:47:20.388 --> 00:47:24.085
If we wash that dress tonight,
nobody would notice it tomorrow.

00:47:24.759 --> 00:47:26.522
You could put this on.

00:47:28.262 --> 00:47:30.958
Take your dress and put it
to soak in the bathtub.

00:47:31.198 --> 00:47:34.725
Come back here and sit on the bed,
and we'll have a talk.

00:47:36.037 --> 00:47:39.063
I told you today
I didn't need a governess.

00:47:39.273 --> 00:47:41.366
Well, maybe I do.

00:48:11.839 --> 00:48:14.399
Gretl, are you scared?

00:48:17.912 --> 00:48:20.176
You're not frightened
of a storm, are you?

00:48:20.414 --> 00:48:22.678
You just stay right here with me.

00:48:23.851 --> 00:48:28.083
- Where are the others?
- They're asleep. They're not scared.

00:48:32.493 --> 00:48:34.324
Oh, no? Look.

00:48:35.863 --> 00:48:37.831
All right, up here on the bed.

00:48:38.132 --> 00:48:40.828
- Really?
- Well, just this once. Come on.

00:48:41.936 --> 00:48:46.270
- Now we'll wait for the boys.
- You won't see them. Boys are brave.

00:48:52.346 --> 00:48:54.143
You weren't scared, were you?

00:48:54.682 --> 00:48:57.879
Oh, no. We just wanted
to be sure that you weren't.

00:48:58.986 --> 00:49:02.012
- That's very thoughtful of you.
- It wasn't my idea.

00:49:02.323 --> 00:49:04.154
It was Kurt's!

00:49:04.392 --> 00:49:06.986
Kurt! That's the one I left out!
God bless Kurt.

00:49:09.797 --> 00:49:11.560
Why does it do that?

00:49:11.799 --> 00:49:15.633
The lightning talks to the thunder,
and the thunder answers.

00:49:15.870 --> 00:49:18.361
- But lightning must be nasty.
- Not really.

00:49:18.639 --> 00:49:20.903
Why does the thunder get so angry?

00:49:21.175 --> 00:49:23.302
It makes me want to cry.

00:49:25.179 --> 00:49:29.377
Whenever I'm feeling unhappy,
I just try to think of nice things.

00:49:29.583 --> 00:49:31.414
What kind of things?

00:49:32.186 --> 00:49:34.154
Well, let me see. Nice things...

00:49:34.388 --> 00:49:35.480
Daffodils.

00:49:36.757 --> 00:49:38.156
Green meadows.

00:49:38.559 --> 00:49:40.823
Skies full of stars.

00:49:41.028 --> 00:49:44.225
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>and whiskers on kittens</i>

00:49:44.432 --> 00:49:47.560
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:49:47.768 --> 00:49:50.931
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:49:51.205 --> 00:49:55.198
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:49:57.778 --> 00:50:00.576
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:50:00.848 --> 00:50:04.045
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:50:04.285 --> 00:50:07.220
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:50:07.455 --> 00:50:11.289
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:12.560 --> 00:50:15.290
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:50:15.563 --> 00:50:18.760
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:50:19.033 --> 00:50:22.093
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:50:22.369 --> 00:50:25.736
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:25.940 --> 00:50:27.635
<i>When the dog bites</i>

00:50:27.875 --> 00:50:29.536
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:50:29.777 --> 00:50:32.041
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:50:32.279 --> 00:50:35.646
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:50:35.916 --> 00:50:42.754
<i>And then I don't feel so bad</i>

00:50:43.491 --> 00:50:45.152
- Does it work?
- Of course.

00:50:45.459 --> 00:50:47.393
- What do you like?
- Pussy willow!

00:50:48.095 --> 00:50:50.325
- Christmas!
- Bunny rabbits!

00:50:50.564 --> 00:50:52.225
Snakes!

00:50:52.500 --> 00:50:54.627
- Chocolate icing!
- No school!

00:50:54.935 --> 00:50:56.061
Pillow fights!

00:50:56.337 --> 00:50:58.328
- Telegrams!
- Birthday presents!

00:50:58.739 --> 00:51:01.105
- Any presents!
- Ladybugs!

00:51:02.610 --> 00:51:03.941
A good sneeze!

00:51:04.245 --> 00:51:05.974
Gesundheit!

00:51:06.280 --> 00:51:07.508
See what fun it is?

00:51:07.748 --> 00:51:10.683
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

00:51:10.951 --> 00:51:13.818
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:51:14.088 --> 00:51:17.080
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:51:17.324 --> 00:51:20.157
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:23.597 --> 00:51:26.430
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:51:26.667 --> 00:51:29.534
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:51:29.770 --> 00:51:32.705
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:51:32.973 --> 00:51:36.465
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:37.444 --> 00:51:38.934
Together.

00:51:39.213 --> 00:51:41.977
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:51:42.216 --> 00:51:45.117
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:51:45.352 --> 00:51:48.344
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:51:48.622 --> 00:51:51.887
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:52.193 --> 00:51:54.320
<i>When the dog bi...</i>

00:51:54.528 --> 00:51:56.496
Dog bites.

00:52:03.137 --> 00:52:04.365
Hello.

00:52:04.572 --> 00:52:08.736
Fräulein, did I not tell you that
bedtime is to be strictly observed?

00:52:09.043 --> 00:52:11.739
The children were upset
by the storm, so l...

00:52:13.147 --> 00:52:14.136
You did, sir.

00:52:14.348 --> 00:52:18.546
Do you, or do you not, have difficulty
remembering such simple instructions?

00:52:19.853 --> 00:52:21.480
Only during thunderstorms.

00:52:23.991 --> 00:52:25.481
Liesl?

00:52:25.726 --> 00:52:27.921
I don't recall seeing you
after dinner.

00:52:28.529 --> 00:52:30.258
Really? As a matter of fact...

00:52:30.531 --> 00:52:31.759
Yes?

00:52:32.566 --> 00:52:33.726
Well, I was...

00:52:34.001 --> 00:52:36.060
What she would like to say...

00:52:36.270 --> 00:52:39.171
...is that she and I have
been getting acquainted tonight.

00:52:39.373 --> 00:52:44.242
It's too late to go into that. You
heard your father. Go back to bed.

00:52:48.882 --> 00:52:50.281
Fräulein...

00:52:50.584 --> 00:52:54.611
...you have managed to remember
I'm leaving in the morning?

00:52:55.723 --> 00:53:00.251
Is it also possible you remember the
first rule in this house is discipline?

00:53:01.929 --> 00:53:04.420
Then I trust that before I return...

00:53:04.932 --> 00:53:06.695
...you'll have acquired some?

00:53:08.068 --> 00:53:09.433
Captain?

00:53:10.404 --> 00:53:14.306
Could I talk to you about clothes
for the children for when they play?

00:53:14.575 --> 00:53:17.271
- If I could have some material.
- You are many things.

00:53:17.544 --> 00:53:19.705
Not the least of which is repetitious.

00:53:19.913 --> 00:53:22.074
- But they're children!
- Yes.

00:53:22.316 --> 00:53:24.079
And I'm their father.

00:53:24.652 --> 00:53:25.880
Good night.

00:53:50.144 --> 00:53:55.980
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:54:07.494 --> 00:54:11.021
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:54:11.265 --> 00:54:13.756
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:54:14.001 --> 00:54:17.300
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:54:17.504 --> 00:54:19.631
<i>And then I don't feel...</i>

00:54:19.873 --> 00:54:26.802
<i>...so bad</i>

00:54:50.804 --> 00:54:53.500
Children, over here. See!

00:54:57.144 --> 00:54:58.509
Come on.

00:56:21.562 --> 00:56:22.790
Fräulein Maria?

00:56:23.063 --> 00:56:24.963
Can we do this every day?

00:56:25.265 --> 00:56:28.462
- Don't you think you'd get tired of it?
- I suppose so.

00:56:28.802 --> 00:56:30.064
Every other day?

00:56:30.270 --> 00:56:34.900
I haven't had so much fun since we put
glue on Fräulein Josephine's toothbrush.

00:56:35.108 --> 00:56:39.010
I can't understand how children
as nice as you can play such tricks.

00:56:39.279 --> 00:56:41.110
- It's easy.
- But why do it?

00:56:41.315 --> 00:56:43.749
How else can we get
Father's attention?

00:56:44.518 --> 00:56:46.110
Oh, I see.

00:56:47.454 --> 00:56:49.649
We'll have to think about that one.

00:56:51.825 --> 00:56:53.452
All right, over here.

00:56:53.660 --> 00:56:55.093
What are we going to do?

00:56:55.329 --> 00:56:57.297
Think of a song for the baroness.

00:56:57.531 --> 00:56:59.499
Father doesn't like us to sing.

00:56:59.766 --> 00:57:03.327
Perhaps we can change his mind.
Now, what songs do you know?

00:57:03.604 --> 00:57:05.765
We don't know any songs.

00:57:06.006 --> 00:57:08.668
- Not any?
- We don't even know how to sing.

00:57:10.344 --> 00:57:12.505
Let's not lose time. You must learn.

00:57:12.779 --> 00:57:14.508
But how?

00:57:18.819 --> 00:57:22.778
<i>Let's start at the very beginning</i>

00:57:22.990 --> 00:57:26.357
<i>A very good place to start</i>

00:57:26.560 --> 00:57:28.494
<i>When you read you begin with</i>

00:57:28.729 --> 00:57:29.957
<i>A, B, C</i>

00:57:30.163 --> 00:57:34.497
<i>When you sing, you begin with</i>
<i>Do-Re-Mi</i>

00:57:34.735 --> 00:57:36.362
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:36.637 --> 00:57:37.968
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:38.205 --> 00:57:42.039
<i>The first three notes</i>
<i>Just happen to be</i>

00:57:42.309 --> 00:57:44.072
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:44.311 --> 00:57:45.573
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:45.812 --> 00:57:49.748
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti</i>

00:57:50.417 --> 00:57:52.851
Let's see if I can make it easier.

00:57:56.256 --> 00:57:59.919
<i>"Doe," a deer</i>
<i>A female deer</i>

00:58:00.160 --> 00:58:03.721
<i>"Ray," a drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:03.997 --> 00:58:07.763
<i>"Me," a name I call myself</i>

00:58:08.035 --> 00:58:11.732
<i>"Far," a long long way to run</i>

00:58:12.005 --> 00:58:15.771
<i>"Sew," a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:16.076 --> 00:58:19.910
<i>"La," a note to follow sew</i>

00:58:20.180 --> 00:58:23.115
<i>"Tea," a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:23.584 --> 00:58:27.680
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:58:28.188 --> 00:58:31.749
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:32.025 --> 00:58:35.222
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:35.462 --> 00:58:38.761
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

00:58:39.032 --> 00:58:42.126
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

00:58:42.636 --> 00:58:46.094
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:46.306 --> 00:58:49.639
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

00:58:50.077 --> 00:58:52.944
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:53.213 --> 00:58:55.477
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

00:58:55.716 --> 00:58:59.152
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:59.419 --> 00:59:02.479
<i>Ray, a drop of golden sun</i>

00:59:02.956 --> 00:59:06.153
<i>Me, a name I call myself</i>

00:59:06.426 --> 00:59:09.486
<i>Far, a long long way to run</i>

00:59:09.763 --> 00:59:12.994
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:59:13.300 --> 00:59:16.667
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

00:59:16.937 --> 00:59:19.565
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:59:19.773 --> 00:59:23.834
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:59:24.244 --> 00:59:27.338
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do</i>

00:59:27.781 --> 00:59:32.343
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

00:59:32.619 --> 00:59:35.850
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

00:59:36.123 --> 00:59:38.250
...by mixing them up. Like this:

00:59:39.493 --> 00:59:44.988
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:45.198 --> 00:59:46.290
Can you do that?

00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:51.995
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:52.205 --> 00:59:57.871
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

00:59:58.178 --> 01:00:03.480
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:03.684 --> 01:00:05.447
Now, put it all together.

01:00:05.652 --> 01:00:12.285
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:00:12.526 --> 01:00:18.487
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:19.066 --> 01:00:21.660
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

01:00:21.902 --> 01:00:24.871
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

01:00:25.138 --> 01:00:26.400
Like this:

01:00:26.640 --> 01:00:33.204
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:33.480 --> 01:00:39.077
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:39.352 --> 01:00:40.319
Together!

01:00:40.520 --> 01:00:47.221
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:47.427 --> 01:00:54.094
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:54.501 --> 01:00:57.868
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

01:00:58.138 --> 01:01:01.335
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

01:01:01.608 --> 01:01:04.839
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

01:01:05.045 --> 01:01:08.105
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

01:01:08.348 --> 01:01:11.715
<i>- Sew</i>
<i>- A needle pulling thread</i>

01:01:12.018 --> 01:01:15.283
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

01:01:15.489 --> 01:01:18.481
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:01:18.692 --> 01:01:22.560
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

01:01:40.147 --> 01:01:46.416
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:01:46.987 --> 01:01:53.483
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:01:54.060 --> 01:01:57.223
<i>Doe</i>
<i>A deer, a female deer</i>

01:01:57.497 --> 01:02:01.024
<i>Ray</i>
<i>A drop of golden sun</i>

01:02:01.234 --> 01:02:04.692
<i>Me</i>
<i>A name I call myself</i>

01:02:04.938 --> 01:02:08.101
<i>Far</i>
<i>A long long way to run</i>

01:02:08.375 --> 01:02:11.538
<i>Sew</i>
<i>A needle pulling thread</i>

01:02:11.745 --> 01:02:14.942
<i>La</i>
<i>A note to follow sew</i>

01:02:15.549 --> 01:02:18.177
<i>Tea</i>
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:02:18.418 --> 01:02:22.377
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

01:02:22.589 --> 01:02:29.427
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:02:29.696 --> 01:02:34.190
<i>So-do-la-fa-ti</i>

01:02:34.434 --> 01:02:36.061
<i>La-so</i>

01:02:39.606 --> 01:02:45.408
<i>Ti-do</i>

01:02:45.612 --> 01:02:47.102
<i>So-do</i>

01:03:00.560 --> 01:03:03.654
The mountains are magnificent,
really magnificent.

01:03:03.897 --> 01:03:06.559
- I had them put up just for you.
- Oh?

01:03:06.833 --> 01:03:08.994
Even if it's to a height
of 10,000 feet...

01:03:09.269 --> 01:03:12.796
...Georg always believes in
"rising to the occasion."

01:03:13.073 --> 01:03:15.337
Improve the jokes
or I'll disinvite you.

01:03:15.942 --> 01:03:18.502
You didn't invite me.
I invited myself.

01:03:18.778 --> 01:03:21.303
- Naturally.
- You needed a chaperone...

01:03:21.581 --> 01:03:24.311
...and I needed a place
where the cuisine is superb...

01:03:24.584 --> 01:03:27.178
...the wine cellar unexcelled...

01:03:27.487 --> 01:03:30.081
...and the price perfect.

01:03:30.457 --> 01:03:32.288
Max, you are outrageous.

01:03:32.525 --> 01:03:36.518
Not at all.
I'm a very charming sponge.

01:03:39.165 --> 01:03:40.291
Listen.

01:03:42.636 --> 01:03:44.866
That's the Klopmann Monastery Choir.

01:03:47.874 --> 01:03:49.501
They're good.

01:03:50.543 --> 01:03:52.170
Very good.

01:03:52.979 --> 01:03:55.641
I must explore this area
in the next few days.

01:03:55.849 --> 01:03:59.307
Somewhere, a hungry singing group
is waiting for Max Detweiler...

01:03:59.552 --> 01:04:03.852
...to pluck it out and make it famous
at the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:04:04.057 --> 01:04:07.356
- They get fame, you get money.
- It's unfair, I admit it.

01:04:07.627 --> 01:04:11.996
But someday that'll be changed.
I shall get the fame too.

01:04:19.039 --> 01:04:21.200
Good heavens, what's this?

01:04:22.642 --> 01:04:24.974
It's nothing.
Just some local urchins.

01:04:40.193 --> 01:04:44.095
This really is exciting for me, Georg.
Being here with you.

01:04:44.931 --> 01:04:47.491
Trees, lakes,
you've seen them before.

01:04:47.767 --> 01:04:50.361
That is not what I mean,
and you know it.

01:04:50.603 --> 01:04:54.562
- You mean me? I'm exciting?
- Is that so impossible?

01:04:54.841 --> 01:04:57.867
No, just highly improbable.

01:04:58.111 --> 01:05:02.275
- There you go, running yourself down.
- Well, I'm a dangerous driver.

01:05:06.052 --> 01:05:09.749
You're much less of a riddle
when I see you here, Georg.

01:05:09.956 --> 01:05:12.789
- In my natural habitat?
- Yes, exactly.

01:05:13.093 --> 01:05:15.220
Are you saying that I'm more
at home...

01:05:15.462 --> 01:05:19.455
...among the birds and the flowers
and the wind that moves...

01:05:19.733 --> 01:05:21.894
...through the trees
like a restless sea?

01:05:22.135 --> 01:05:23.727
How poetic.

01:05:23.937 --> 01:05:25.802
Yes, it was rather, wasn't it?

01:05:26.940 --> 01:05:32.071
More at home here than in Vienna
in all your glittering salons...

01:05:32.278 --> 01:05:36.647
...gossiping gaily with bores I
detest, soaking myself in champagne...

01:05:36.950 --> 01:05:40.647
...stumbling about to waltzes
by Strausses I can't even remember?

01:05:40.954 --> 01:05:43.081
- Is that what you're saying?
- Yes.

01:05:43.323 --> 01:05:45.621
Now whatever gave you that idea?

01:05:48.995 --> 01:05:52.897
Oh, I do like it here, Georg.
It's so lovely and peaceful.

01:05:53.233 --> 01:05:55.167
How can you leave it so often?

01:05:55.435 --> 01:05:58.268
Oh, pretending to be madly active,
I suppose.

01:05:58.505 --> 01:06:01.770
Activity suggests a life
filled with purpose.

01:06:02.509 --> 01:06:04.773
Could it be running away
from memories?

01:06:07.981 --> 01:06:11.917
Or perhaps just searching
for a reason to stay.

01:06:12.585 --> 01:06:16.077
I hope that's why you've been
coming to Vienna so often.

01:06:16.756 --> 01:06:21.090
- Were there other distractions?
- I'd hardly call you a distraction.

01:06:21.327 --> 01:06:23.989
Well, what would you call me, Georg?

01:06:26.266 --> 01:06:27.528
Lovely...

01:06:28.535 --> 01:06:31.163
...charming, witty, graceful,
the perfect hostess...

01:06:31.371 --> 01:06:34.204
...and, you're going to hate me
for this...

01:06:34.641 --> 01:06:36.700
...in a way, my savior.

01:06:36.976 --> 01:06:38.807
Oh, how unromantic.

01:06:39.012 --> 01:06:41.344
I'd be an ungrateful wretch
if I didn't say...

01:06:41.614 --> 01:06:44.845
...that you brought some meaning back
into my life.

01:06:46.686 --> 01:06:49.450
I am amusing, I suppose.

01:06:49.689 --> 01:06:54.456
I have the finest couturier in Vienna
and a glittering circle of friends.

01:06:54.661 --> 01:06:57.789
- I do give some rather gay parties.
- Oh, yes.

01:06:58.031 --> 01:06:59.862
But take all that away...

01:07:00.066 --> 01:07:04.503
...and you have just wealthy,
unattached little me...

01:07:05.171 --> 01:07:07.571
...searching, just like you.

01:07:12.679 --> 01:07:14.374
More strudel, Herr Detweiler?

01:07:14.647 --> 01:07:16.171
- How many have I had?
- Two.

01:07:16.416 --> 01:07:18.350
Make it an uneven three.

01:07:21.654 --> 01:07:24.680
Still eating, Max?
Must be unhappy.

01:07:24.891 --> 01:07:28.850
That mixed quartet I've been trying
to steal away from Sol Hurok...

01:07:29.095 --> 01:07:31.757
- What happened?
...Sascha Petrie stole them first.

01:07:31.998 --> 01:07:33.260
I hate thieves.

01:07:33.533 --> 01:07:36.832
Max, you really must try
and learn to love yourself.

01:07:37.070 --> 01:07:39.402
I had to call Paris, Rome
and Stockholm.

01:07:39.672 --> 01:07:43.233
- On Georg's telephone, of course.
- How else could I afford it?

01:07:43.710 --> 01:07:48.841
I like rich people, the way they live
and how I live when I'm with them.

01:07:49.182 --> 01:07:51.173
I wonder where the children are.

01:07:51.584 --> 01:07:54.075
They must have heard
I was coming and hid.

01:07:54.354 --> 01:07:56.845
I was hoping they'd be here
to welcome you.

01:07:57.090 --> 01:08:01.584
Max, do step out of character for
a moment and try and be charming.

01:08:10.637 --> 01:08:12.036
Well?

01:08:12.939 --> 01:08:14.133
Well what?

01:08:14.374 --> 01:08:17.275
Have you made up his mind?
Do I hear wedding bells?

01:08:17.544 --> 01:08:19.535
- Pealing madly.
- Marvelous.

01:08:19.779 --> 01:08:22.543
- Not necessarily for me.
- What kind of talk's that?

01:08:22.749 --> 01:08:24.307
None-of-your-business talk.

01:08:24.617 --> 01:08:27.051
I'm terribly fond of him,
so don't toy with us.

01:08:27.320 --> 01:08:30.915
But I'm a child. I like toys.
So tell me everything.

01:08:31.224 --> 01:08:36.287
Come on. Tell me every teensy-weensy,
intimate, disgusting detail.

01:08:37.764 --> 01:08:41.894
Well, let's just say I have a feeling
I may be here on approval.

01:08:42.135 --> 01:08:45.161
- I approve of that. How can you miss?
- Far too easily.

01:08:45.438 --> 01:08:48.669
If I know you, darling,
and I do, you will find a way.

01:08:48.942 --> 01:08:51.433
- He's no ordinary man.
- No, he's rich.

01:08:51.678 --> 01:08:53.942
His wife's death gave him
a great heartache.

01:08:54.147 --> 01:08:57.275
And your husband's death
gave you a great fortune.

01:08:57.483 --> 01:08:59.451
Oh, Max, you really are a beast.

01:08:59.652 --> 01:09:03.679
You and Georg are like family.
That's why I want to see you married.

01:09:03.923 --> 01:09:07.484
We must keep all that lovely money
in the family.

01:09:23.776 --> 01:09:26.711
- What are you doing there?
- Oh, Captain von Trapp.

01:09:26.980 --> 01:09:29.005
I was just looking for...

01:09:29.882 --> 01:09:32.715
I didn't see, I mean,
I didn't know you were...

01:09:33.319 --> 01:09:35.014
Heil Hitler!

01:09:35.722 --> 01:09:37.212
Who are you?

01:09:37.490 --> 01:09:39.720
I have a telegram for Herr Detweiler.

01:09:39.993 --> 01:09:42.723
- I am Herr Detweiler.
- Yes, sir.

01:09:47.800 --> 01:09:50.394
You've delivered your telegram.
Now get out.

01:09:57.176 --> 01:10:00.577
- Georg, he's just a boy.
- Yes, and I'm just an Austrian.

01:10:00.813 --> 01:10:03.577
Things will happen.
Make sure they don't happen to you.

01:10:03.883 --> 01:10:06.545
Max! Don't you ever say that again.

01:10:06.819 --> 01:10:09.014
I have no political convictions.

01:10:09.255 --> 01:10:12.190
- Can I help it if other people do?
- You can help it.

01:10:13.326 --> 01:10:15.487
You must help it.

01:10:25.772 --> 01:10:27.364
Hello?

01:10:30.009 --> 01:10:32.773
You're far away. Where are you?

01:10:33.079 --> 01:10:36.947
In a world that's disappearing,
I'm afraid.

01:10:37.784 --> 01:10:41.379
Is there any way I could bring you
back to the world I'm in?

01:11:07.313 --> 01:11:09.804
- Father! Father!
- There's your father!

01:11:10.616 --> 01:11:13.244
Oh, captain, you're home!

01:11:21.627 --> 01:11:24.289
Come out of that water at once!

01:11:33.406 --> 01:11:35.601
Oh, you must be Baroness Schraeder.

01:11:40.913 --> 01:11:43.905
I'm soaked to the skin!

01:11:55.862 --> 01:11:57.261
Straight line!

01:12:11.944 --> 01:12:14.344
This is Baroness Schraeder.

01:12:16.949 --> 01:12:18.712
And these...

01:12:18.951 --> 01:12:20.543
...are my children.

01:12:21.654 --> 01:12:23.144
How do you do?

01:12:24.223 --> 01:12:28.956
Go inside, dry off, clean up, change
your clothes and report back here!

01:12:33.966 --> 01:12:36.059
Fräulein, you will stay here, please!

01:12:37.804 --> 01:12:41.365
I think I'd better go see
what Max is up to.

01:12:51.584 --> 01:12:53.347
Now, fräulein...

01:12:55.254 --> 01:12:57.313
...I want a truthful answer.

01:12:57.723 --> 01:12:59.190
Yes, captain.

01:12:59.492 --> 01:13:03.553
Is it possible,
or could I have just imagined it?

01:13:05.064 --> 01:13:09.558
Have my children, by any chance,
been climbing trees today?

01:13:10.036 --> 01:13:11.196
Yes, captain.

01:13:12.271 --> 01:13:13.602
I see.

01:13:14.173 --> 01:13:18.667
And where, may I ask,
did they get these...

01:13:18.945 --> 01:13:21.004
- Play clothes.
- Is that what they are?

01:13:21.214 --> 01:13:24.615
I made them from the drapes
that used to hang in my bedroom.

01:13:25.418 --> 01:13:27.545
- Drapes?
- They have plenty of wear left.

01:13:27.753 --> 01:13:29.687
We've been everywhere in them.

01:13:29.922 --> 01:13:34.382
Are you telling me that my children
have been roaming about Salzburg...

01:13:34.594 --> 01:13:37.961
...dressed up in nothing
but some old drapes?

01:13:38.197 --> 01:13:39.858
And having a marvelous time!

01:13:40.066 --> 01:13:43.297
- They have uniforms.
- Forgive me, straitjackets.

01:13:43.536 --> 01:13:46.300
They can't be children
if they worry about clothes...

01:13:46.572 --> 01:13:47.698
They don't complain.

01:13:47.940 --> 01:13:50.636
They don't dare.
They love you too much and fear...

01:13:50.877 --> 01:13:52.435
Don't discuss my children.

01:13:52.645 --> 01:13:54.579
You've got to hear, you're
never home...

01:13:54.780 --> 01:13:56.304
I don't want to hear more!

01:13:56.549 --> 01:13:59.040
I know you don't, but you've got to!

01:13:59.819 --> 01:14:01.980
- Liesl's not a child.
- Not one word...

01:14:02.255 --> 01:14:05.122
Soon she'll be a woman
and you won't even know her.

01:14:05.391 --> 01:14:08.451
Friedrich wants to be a man
but you're not here to show...

01:14:08.728 --> 01:14:10.059
Don't you dare tell me...

01:14:10.296 --> 01:14:13.561
Brigitta could tell you about him.
She notices everything.

01:14:13.799 --> 01:14:16.927
Kurt acts tough to hide the pain
when you ignore him...

01:14:17.136 --> 01:14:18.660
...the way you do all of them.

01:14:18.938 --> 01:14:21.338
Louisa, I don't know about yet.

01:14:21.607 --> 01:14:24.804
The little ones just want love.
Please, love them all.

01:14:25.077 --> 01:14:26.601
I don't care to hear more.

01:14:26.846 --> 01:14:30.942
- I am not finished yet, captain!
- Oh, yes, you are, captain!

01:14:32.485 --> 01:14:33.645
Fräulein.

01:14:34.954 --> 01:14:39.084
Now, you will pack
your things this minute...

01:14:39.292 --> 01:14:41.783
...and return to the abbey.

01:14:44.430 --> 01:14:45.761
What's that?

01:14:47.500 --> 01:14:48.524
It's singing.

01:14:49.168 --> 01:14:51.966
Yes, I realize it's singing.
But who is singing?

01:14:52.939 --> 01:14:54.497
The children.

01:14:57.376 --> 01:14:58.707
The children?

01:14:59.278 --> 01:15:02.008
I taught them something to sing
for the baroness.

01:15:07.653 --> 01:15:13.683
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

01:15:13.960 --> 01:15:16.520
<i>Every song that it hears</i>

01:15:16.796 --> 01:15:22.234
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

01:15:22.501 --> 01:15:25.629
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

01:15:25.871 --> 01:15:27.304
<i>To the trees</i>

01:15:27.540 --> 01:15:32.477
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

01:15:32.678 --> 01:15:37.308
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

01:15:37.583 --> 01:15:41.485
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

01:15:41.754 --> 01:15:44.689
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

01:15:44.991 --> 01:15:46.356
<i>On its way</i>

01:15:46.592 --> 01:15:51.029
<i>To sing through the night</i>

01:15:51.230 --> 01:15:56.896
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

01:15:57.169 --> 01:16:01.663
<i>I go to the hills</i>

01:16:01.874 --> 01:16:08.109
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

01:16:08.381 --> 01:16:12.078
<i>I know I will hear</i>

01:16:12.351 --> 01:16:18.119
<i>What I've heard before</i>

01:16:18.958 --> 01:16:23.190
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

01:16:23.429 --> 01:16:30.392
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:16:31.270 --> 01:16:36.469
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

01:16:36.709 --> 01:16:44.809
<i>...once more</i>

01:17:18.084 --> 01:17:19.847
Edelweiss!

01:17:23.823 --> 01:17:26.986
You never told me how enchanting
your children are.

01:17:35.601 --> 01:17:37.159
Don't go away.

01:17:42.274 --> 01:17:43.673
Fräulein.

01:17:47.012 --> 01:17:48.206
I...

01:17:49.682 --> 01:17:52.480
...behaved badly. I apologize.

01:17:54.220 --> 01:17:57.815
I'm far too outspoken.
It's one of my worst faults.

01:17:58.224 --> 01:17:59.691
You were right.

01:18:02.161 --> 01:18:04.061
I don't know my children.

01:18:05.364 --> 01:18:09.494
There's still time, captain.
They want so much to be close to you.

01:18:09.835 --> 01:18:13.703
And you brought music back
into the house.

01:18:15.040 --> 01:18:16.473
I'd forgotten.

01:18:19.211 --> 01:18:20.542
Fräulein.

01:18:23.048 --> 01:18:24.310
I want you to stay.

01:18:28.320 --> 01:18:31.050
I ask you to stay.

01:18:32.892 --> 01:18:36.384
- If I could be of any help.
- You have already.

01:18:36.996 --> 01:18:38.054
More than you know.

01:18:57.783 --> 01:18:59.114
Marta.

01:18:59.852 --> 01:19:01.080
Curtain!

01:19:03.756 --> 01:19:07.089
<i>High on a hill was a lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:08.594 --> 01:19:11.859
<i>Loud was the voice</i>
<i>Of the lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:13.365 --> 01:19:16.630
<i>Folks in a town</i>
<i>That was quite remote heard</i>

01:19:18.204 --> 01:19:21.435
<i>Lusty and clear</i>
<i>From the goatherd's throat heard</i>

01:19:32.952 --> 01:19:35.819
Marta. Marta!

01:19:38.224 --> 01:19:40.215
Gretl, the prince!

01:19:41.961 --> 01:19:45.419
<i>A prince on the bridge</i>
<i>Of a castle moat heard</i>

01:19:46.899 --> 01:19:49.231
<i>Men on a road</i>
<i>With a load to tote heard</i>

01:19:51.737 --> 01:19:55.002
<i>Men in the midst</i>
<i>Of a table d'hôte heard</i>

01:19:56.342 --> 01:19:59.607
<i>Men drinking beer</i>
<i>With the foam afloat heard</i>

01:20:10.689 --> 01:20:13.817
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:20:15.461 --> 01:20:18.794
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:20:19.965 --> 01:20:23.366
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:20:24.870 --> 01:20:28.169
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:14.753 --> 01:21:18.018
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:21:19.558 --> 01:21:22.823
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:21:24.163 --> 01:21:27.599
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:21:29.068 --> 01:21:32.196
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:33.906 --> 01:21:35.533
<i>Happy are they</i>

01:21:38.510 --> 01:21:41.775
<i>Soon the duet will become a trio</i>

01:22:06.271 --> 01:22:07.863
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

01:22:08.073 --> 01:22:09.563
Very good!

01:22:11.377 --> 01:22:13.277
Wonderful!

01:22:13.879 --> 01:22:17.042
- Can we keep the puppets, Uncle Max?
- Yes, can we?

01:22:17.249 --> 01:22:19.274
Of course you may, my darlings.

01:22:19.485 --> 01:22:23.717
Why else did I tell Professor Kohner
to send the bill to your father?

01:22:27.459 --> 01:22:29.120
Well done, fräulein.

01:22:31.630 --> 01:22:33.598
I really am very much impressed.

01:22:33.799 --> 01:22:35.790
They're your children, captain.

01:22:43.008 --> 01:22:45.306
My dear, is there anything
you can't do?

01:22:45.577 --> 01:22:47.909
Well, I'm not sure
I'll make a good nun.

01:22:48.147 --> 01:22:51.241
If you have any problems,
I'd be happy to help you.

01:22:54.353 --> 01:22:55.786
Attention, everyone!

01:22:55.988 --> 01:22:59.446
I have an announcement to make.
Surprise! Surprise!

01:22:59.691 --> 01:23:01.989
Today, after a long
and desperate search...

01:23:02.261 --> 01:23:07.255
...I have found a most exciting
entry for the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:23:07.466 --> 01:23:09.297
Congratulations, Max.

01:23:09.535 --> 01:23:12.504
And who will you
be exploiting this time?

01:23:14.306 --> 01:23:17.503
- The Saint Ignatius Choir?
- Guess again.

01:23:18.210 --> 01:23:22.146
Well, let me see now.
The Klopmann Choir?

01:23:22.381 --> 01:23:24.781
- No, no, no, no.
- No, no?

01:23:24.983 --> 01:23:26.177
Tell us.

01:23:26.385 --> 01:23:29.843
A singing group all in one family.
You'll never guess, Georg.

01:23:30.122 --> 01:23:33.023
What a charming idea!

01:23:33.225 --> 01:23:35.022
Whose family?

01:23:35.894 --> 01:23:37.521
Yours.

01:23:37.729 --> 01:23:40.061
They'll be the talk of the festival.

01:23:42.901 --> 01:23:45.893
- Well, now, what's so funny?
- You are, Max.

01:23:46.171 --> 01:23:49.299
You're expensive, but very funny.

01:23:50.042 --> 01:23:52.374
- They'll be a sensation!
- No, Max.

01:23:52.644 --> 01:23:54.839
It's a wonderful idea.
Fresh, original.

01:23:55.047 --> 01:23:59.848
Max! My children
do not sing in public.

01:24:00.519 --> 01:24:02.487
You can't blame me for trying.

01:24:02.688 --> 01:24:05.680
Children, who shall we hear
from next?

01:24:08.494 --> 01:24:09.654
Who?

01:24:15.834 --> 01:24:17.028
Yes.

01:24:19.905 --> 01:24:21.839
The vote is unanimous.

01:24:22.674 --> 01:24:24.232
You, captain.

01:24:24.510 --> 01:24:25.704
Me?

01:24:26.545 --> 01:24:28.843
- I don't understand.
- Please.

01:24:35.053 --> 01:24:37.180
No, no, no, no.

01:24:37.456 --> 01:24:39.515
I'm told that you were quite good.

01:24:39.725 --> 01:24:43.024
- That was a very, very long time ago.
- I remember, Father.

01:24:43.262 --> 01:24:46.129
- Play us something we know.
- Oh, please, Father.

01:24:49.067 --> 01:24:50.125
Well...

01:25:00.379 --> 01:25:02.540
- Why didn't you tell me?
- What?

01:25:02.814 --> 01:25:05.112
To bring along my harmonica.

01:25:07.452 --> 01:25:09.579
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:11.156 --> 01:25:13.454
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:14.560 --> 01:25:20.760
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:25:20.999 --> 01:25:24.059
<i>Small and white</i>

01:25:24.903 --> 01:25:28.270
<i>Clean and bright</i>

01:25:28.473 --> 01:25:31.306
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:25:31.510 --> 01:25:35.344
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:25:35.614 --> 01:25:37.912
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:25:38.183 --> 01:25:42.313
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:25:42.521 --> 01:25:48.858
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:25:49.828 --> 01:25:53.525
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:53.765 --> 01:25:56.359
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:57.035 --> 01:26:04.305
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:26:08.680 --> 01:26:11.877
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:12.184 --> 01:26:15.676
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:15.887 --> 01:26:22.292
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:26:22.527 --> 01:26:26.054
<i>- Small and white</i>
<i>- Small and white</i>

01:26:26.331 --> 01:26:29.789
<i>- Clean and bright</i>
<i>- Clean and bright</i>

01:26:30.002 --> 01:26:32.493
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:26:32.738 --> 01:26:36.367
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:26:36.842 --> 01:26:38.969
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:26:39.177 --> 01:26:43.341
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:26:43.582 --> 01:26:50.647
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:26:50.889 --> 01:26:54.518
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:54.760 --> 01:26:57.422
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:58.030 --> 01:27:07.928
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:27:17.215 --> 01:27:20.878
Anytime you say the word, Georg,
you can be part of my new act:

01:27:21.086 --> 01:27:23.577
The von Trapp Family Singers.

01:27:24.690 --> 01:27:27.181
I have a wonderful idea, Georg.

01:27:27.426 --> 01:27:29.894
Let's really fill this house
with music.

01:27:30.128 --> 01:27:33.097
You must give a grand
and glorious party for me.

01:27:33.365 --> 01:27:36.061
- A party?
- Yes, Father, please!

01:27:36.268 --> 01:27:38.634
It's high time
I met all your friends...

01:27:38.937 --> 01:27:41.428
...and they met me.
Don't you agree?

01:27:41.707 --> 01:27:43.937
- I see what you mean.
- Oh, please!

01:27:44.209 --> 01:27:47.372
Children, it's bedtime.
Come now, say good night.

01:27:48.313 --> 01:27:49.610
Good night, Father.

01:27:49.815 --> 01:27:52.648
- Good night.
- Good night, Baroness Schraeder.

01:27:52.884 --> 01:27:54.442
Good night, Father.

01:27:57.422 --> 01:27:59.253
Good night, Uncle Max.

01:28:01.159 --> 01:28:04.322
It'll be my first party, Father!

01:28:36.862 --> 01:28:39.490
- Captain.
- Herr Zeller. Baroness Schraeder.

01:28:39.698 --> 01:28:42.826
- Good evening, Herr Zeller.
- Baroness.

01:28:44.136 --> 01:28:46.604
How do you do? Good evening.

01:29:07.225 --> 01:29:10.661
Did you notice the obvious
display of the Austrian flag?

01:29:17.736 --> 01:29:19.533
The women look so beautiful.

01:29:19.805 --> 01:29:21.136
I think they look ugly.

01:29:21.406 --> 01:29:23.237
You're just scared of them.

01:29:23.475 --> 01:29:25.705
Silly, only grown-up men fear women.

01:29:26.311 --> 01:29:29.872
- I think the men look beautiful.
- How would you know?

01:29:47.165 --> 01:29:49.190
Liesl, who are you dancing with?

01:29:49.401 --> 01:29:51.028
Nobody.

01:29:51.837 --> 01:29:53.737
Oh, yes, you are.

01:29:56.208 --> 01:29:57.698
May I have this dance?

01:29:57.909 --> 01:30:00.400
I'd be delighted, young man.

01:30:07.185 --> 01:30:09.847
Why didn't you tell me
you could dance?

01:30:10.088 --> 01:30:15.025
We feared you'd make us all dance.
The von Trapp Family Dancers.

01:30:19.431 --> 01:30:21.126
What are they playing?

01:30:21.366 --> 01:30:23.994
It's the Laendler.
An Austrian folk dance.

01:30:24.202 --> 01:30:27.365
- Show me.
- I haven't danced since I was little.

01:30:27.572 --> 01:30:29.540
You remember. Please?

01:30:29.808 --> 01:30:31.742
- Well...
- Please.

01:30:31.977 --> 01:30:34.207
All right. Come on over here.

01:30:34.713 --> 01:30:37.546
Now you bow and I curtsy.

01:30:38.483 --> 01:30:41.418
- Like this?
- Fine. Now we go for a little walk.

01:30:41.653 --> 01:30:44.315
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:30:44.623 --> 01:30:49.219
One, two, three, step together.
Now, step hop, step hop.

01:30:49.461 --> 01:30:52.123
Now turn under. Not quite.

01:30:52.330 --> 01:30:56.289
This way. Hop step, hop.
And under.

01:30:56.968 --> 01:30:58.663
Kurt, we'll have to practice.

01:30:58.904 --> 01:31:00.394
Do allow me, will you?

01:32:28.693 --> 01:32:30.558
I don't remember anymore.

01:32:32.731 --> 01:32:34.926
- Your face is all red.
- Is it?

01:32:36.267 --> 01:32:38.360
I don't suppose I'm used to dancing.

01:32:41.072 --> 01:32:43.063
Why, that was beautifully done.

01:32:43.341 --> 01:32:45.241
What a lovely couple you make.

01:32:45.443 --> 01:32:47.570
It's time the children
said good night.

01:32:47.846 --> 01:32:49.177
We'll be in the hall.

01:32:49.414 --> 01:32:52.281
- We have something special prepared.
- Right!

01:32:52.584 --> 01:32:53.744
Yes, come on!

01:33:00.592 --> 01:33:02.924
All that needless worrying, Georg.

01:33:03.194 --> 01:33:06.220
You thought you wouldn't find
a friend at the party.

01:33:09.134 --> 01:33:12.729
- A bit chilly out tonight, isn't it?
- Oh, I don't know.

01:33:12.937 --> 01:33:14.962
It seemed rather warm to me.

01:33:19.144 --> 01:33:20.372
Ladies and gentlemen.

01:33:21.112 --> 01:33:25.208
The children of Captain von Trapp
wish to say good night to you.

01:33:39.330 --> 01:33:43.232
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

01:33:43.435 --> 01:33:47.166
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

01:33:47.439 --> 01:33:51.466
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

01:33:51.676 --> 01:33:54.110
<i>Is popping up to say "coo-coo"</i>

01:33:54.345 --> 01:33:56.006
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:56.281 --> 01:33:57.509
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:57.749 --> 01:33:59.910
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

01:34:00.118 --> 01:34:01.483
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

01:34:01.753 --> 01:34:04.813
<i>To say goodbye</i>

01:34:05.023 --> 01:34:10.325
<i>To you</i>

01:34:13.531 --> 01:34:17.433
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

01:34:17.635 --> 01:34:21.503
<i>I hate to go</i>
<i>And leave this pretty sight</i>

01:34:28.780 --> 01:34:32.113
<i>So long, farewell,</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

01:34:32.784 --> 01:34:36.311
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

01:34:43.661 --> 01:34:47.461
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Au revoir, auf Wiedersehen</i>

01:34:47.732 --> 01:34:51.668
<i>I'd like to stay</i>
<i>And taste my first champagne</i>

01:34:51.903 --> 01:34:54.337
- Yes?
- No.

01:34:58.676 --> 01:35:02.339
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:02.680 --> 01:35:06.639
<i>I leave and heave a sigh</i>
<i>And say goodbye</i>

01:35:06.851 --> 01:35:10.844
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:35:13.892 --> 01:35:16.986
<i>I'm glad to go</i>

01:35:17.228 --> 01:35:20.095
<i>I cannot tell a lie</i>

01:35:20.431 --> 01:35:23.423
<i>I flit, I float</i>

01:35:23.701 --> 01:35:27.159
<i>I fleetly flee, I fly</i>

01:35:37.215 --> 01:35:42.949
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>

01:35:43.188 --> 01:35:46.919
<i>And so must I</i>

01:35:47.125 --> 01:35:49.525
<i>So long</i>

01:35:49.761 --> 01:35:52.321
<i>Farewell</i>

01:35:52.530 --> 01:35:57.934
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:58.203 --> 01:36:03.539
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:04.242 --> 01:36:09.805
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:10.048 --> 01:36:16.920
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:17.121 --> 01:36:25.620
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:30.635 --> 01:36:33.399
Extraordinary!
What they'd do at the festival.

01:36:33.638 --> 01:36:36.129
Young lady,
I must have a word with you.

01:36:37.141 --> 01:36:41.134
Georg, you won't let this girl
get away. She must join the party.

01:36:41.412 --> 01:36:43.812
- No, really l...
- Stop. Stop it now.

01:36:44.082 --> 01:36:47.017
- Georg, please.
- You can if you want to, fräulein.

01:36:47.252 --> 01:36:49.743
I insist.
You will be my dinner partner.

01:36:49.954 --> 01:36:51.854
This is business.
Franz...

01:36:52.123 --> 01:36:55.286
...set another place next to mine
for Fräulein Maria.

01:36:57.462 --> 01:37:00.192
- Whatever you say.
- It appears to be all arranged.

01:37:00.999 --> 01:37:02.864
- It does.
- I'm not suitably dressed.

01:37:03.935 --> 01:37:05.425
You can change. We'll wait.

01:37:09.040 --> 01:37:11.975
Captain, you must be very proud
of your youngsters.

01:37:12.176 --> 01:37:13.040
I am, thank you.

01:37:13.311 --> 01:37:17.873
Is there a more beautiful expression
of what is good in our country...

01:37:18.116 --> 01:37:21.552
...than the innocent voices
of our children?

01:37:21.953 --> 01:37:23.318
Oh, come now, baron.

01:37:23.554 --> 01:37:27.320
Would you have us believe that Austria
holds a monopoly on virtue?

01:37:28.226 --> 01:37:32.356
Herr Zeller, some of us prefer
Austrian voices raised in song...

01:37:32.563 --> 01:37:34.963
...to ugly German threats.

01:37:36.034 --> 01:37:39.663
The ostrich buries his head
in the sand...

01:37:39.871 --> 01:37:42.806
...and sometimes in the flag.

01:37:43.341 --> 01:37:47.539
Perhaps those who would warn you that
the Anschluss is coming, and it is...

01:37:47.812 --> 01:37:51.509
...would get further with you by setting
their words to music.

01:37:51.716 --> 01:37:56.380
If the Nazis take over Austria, you
will be the entire trumpet section.

01:37:56.688 --> 01:37:57.712
You flatter me.

01:37:58.756 --> 01:38:02.658
Oh, how clumsy of me.
I meant to accuse you.

01:38:10.401 --> 01:38:12.892
It's very kind of you
to offer to help me, baroness.

01:38:13.171 --> 01:38:14.729
I'm delighted, Maria.

01:38:15.206 --> 01:38:18.903
I really don't think I have anything
that would be appropriate.

01:38:19.377 --> 01:38:23.507
Now where is that lovely little thing
you were wearing the other evening?

01:38:23.748 --> 01:38:27.047
When the captain couldn't keep
his eyes off you.

01:38:30.421 --> 01:38:32.252
Couldn't keep his eyes off me?

01:38:33.591 --> 01:38:35.388
Come, my dear, we are women.

01:38:35.626 --> 01:38:39.027
Let's not pretend we don't know
when a man notices us.

01:38:39.263 --> 01:38:42.699
- Here we are.
- The captain notices everybody.

01:38:43.267 --> 01:38:45.701
There's no need to feel
so defensive, Maria.

01:38:45.937 --> 01:38:48.405
You are quite attractive, you know.

01:38:48.639 --> 01:38:52.268
The captain would hardly be a man
if he didn't notice you.

01:38:53.878 --> 01:38:56.244
Baroness, I hope you're joking.

01:38:56.714 --> 01:38:57.976
Not at all.

01:38:58.216 --> 01:38:59.808
I've never done a thing to...

01:39:00.084 --> 01:39:01.642
You don't have to, my dear.

01:39:02.286 --> 01:39:07.121
Nothing's more irresistible to a man
than a woman who's in love with him.

01:39:08.393 --> 01:39:10.827
- In love with him?
- Of course.

01:39:11.763 --> 01:39:15.164
What makes it so nice is
he thinks he's in love with you.

01:39:17.902 --> 01:39:19.494
But that's not true.

01:39:19.904 --> 01:39:23.396
Surely you've noticed the way
he looks into your eyes.

01:39:23.674 --> 01:39:28.577
And you know, you blushed in his arms
when you were dancing just now.

01:39:29.814 --> 01:39:31.509
Don't take it to heart.

01:39:31.783 --> 01:39:34.081
He'll get over it soon enough,
I think.

01:39:34.352 --> 01:39:36.320
Men do, you know.

01:39:37.321 --> 01:39:38.413
Then I should go.

01:39:39.757 --> 01:39:41.190
I mustn't stay here.

01:39:51.669 --> 01:39:55.105
- Is there something I can do to help?
- No, nothing.

01:39:56.874 --> 01:39:58.102
Yes.

01:39:59.110 --> 01:40:01.135
Don't say a word to the captain.

01:40:02.780 --> 01:40:06.341
No, I wouldn't dream of it.

01:40:13.124 --> 01:40:14.682
Goodbye, Maria.

01:40:15.493 --> 01:40:18.291
I'm sure you'll make a very fine nun.

01:40:48.326 --> 01:40:50.317
Champagne, darling.

01:40:50.728 --> 01:40:54.721
I feel like celebrating. Cheers.

01:41:00.204 --> 01:41:03.105
- You know something.
- Perhaps.

01:41:03.341 --> 01:41:07.869
If you're so clever, tell me how to
get fräulein to influence Georg.

01:41:08.112 --> 01:41:10.740
I want those children in the festival.

01:41:11.215 --> 01:41:13.513
Elsa, this is important to Austria.

01:41:13.718 --> 01:41:15.413
Wouldn't do you any harm either.

01:41:15.620 --> 01:41:17.212
I thought of that.

01:41:17.455 --> 01:41:19.923
Well, if it's a matter of influence...

01:41:20.124 --> 01:41:23.025
...maybe the one you have
to be talking to is me.

01:44:47.958 --> 01:44:50.188
- Two.
- Three.

01:44:50.460 --> 01:44:51.950
- Four.
- Five.

01:44:53.196 --> 01:44:55.221
- Six.
- Seven.

01:44:55.498 --> 01:44:57.125
Eight.

01:44:57.367 --> 01:44:59.198
- Four.
- Two.

01:45:00.303 --> 01:45:02.134
- Seven.
- Five.

01:45:02.372 --> 01:45:04.567
- Two.
- Six.

01:45:09.212 --> 01:45:11.237
Isn't this fun?

01:45:12.649 --> 01:45:14.981
- Four.
- I'm number five.

01:45:15.251 --> 01:45:17.412
- Oh, yes.
- Eight.

01:45:17.721 --> 01:45:20.087
- Two.
- Four.

01:45:20.490 --> 01:45:21.718
Six.

01:45:24.194 --> 01:45:25.422
Two.

01:45:26.563 --> 01:45:29.532
Baroness Schraeder, do you mind
if we stop now? We're tired.

01:45:29.766 --> 01:45:31.734
Whatever you want, dear.

01:45:32.002 --> 01:45:33.993
We'll do it again tomorrow.

01:45:44.180 --> 01:45:46.341
The country's so restful, isn't it?

01:45:47.384 --> 01:45:49.011
Have some lemonade.

01:45:50.253 --> 01:45:51.686
There must be an easier way.

01:45:53.089 --> 01:45:56.354
I get a fiendish delight thinking
of you as the mother of seven.

01:45:57.293 --> 01:45:59.124
How do you plan to do it?

01:45:59.396 --> 01:46:01.421
Darling, haven't you ever heard...

01:46:01.698 --> 01:46:04.792
...of a delightful little thing
called boarding school?

01:46:05.935 --> 01:46:08.199
Baroness Machiavelli.

01:46:09.539 --> 01:46:11.530
Uncle Max, where's Father?

01:46:11.808 --> 01:46:13.605
I think he's in the house.

01:46:13.810 --> 01:46:16.370
What's the matter
with all you gloomy pussies?

01:46:16.613 --> 01:46:19.411
- Nothing.
- I know. Let's have a rehearsal.

01:46:19.616 --> 01:46:20.514
What for?

01:46:20.717 --> 01:46:23.208
Let's make believe we're on-stage
at the festival.

01:46:23.420 --> 01:46:27.288
- I don't feel like singing.
- Not without Fräulein Maria.

01:46:27.557 --> 01:46:29.957
Liesl, get the guitar.
Come on, Marta.

01:46:30.160 --> 01:46:33.129
Everybody into the group.
Get in your places.

01:46:33.396 --> 01:46:36.160
Now be cheerful, right?
Give us the key, Liesl.

01:46:38.068 --> 01:46:40.730
Now, impress me.

01:46:44.741 --> 01:46:46.072
Gretl, why don't you sing?

01:46:46.342 --> 01:46:48.810
I can't. I've got a sore finger.

01:46:49.846 --> 01:46:52.906
But you sang so beautifully
the night of the party.

01:46:53.116 --> 01:46:55.448
Come on, all of you.
Try something you know.

01:46:55.685 --> 01:46:57.175
Enjoy it. Be cheerful.

01:46:57.454 --> 01:46:59.081
All right, Liesl.

01:47:01.024 --> 01:47:06.428
<i>The hills are alive</i>

01:47:06.663 --> 01:47:14.331
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:15.538 --> 01:47:20.601
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

01:47:20.844 --> 01:47:28.683
<i>For a thousand years</i>

01:47:29.385 --> 01:47:34.789
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

01:47:35.024 --> 01:47:42.726
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:43.066 --> 01:47:45.694
They wanted to sing for me,
bless their hearts.

01:47:46.002 --> 01:47:47.902
That's lovely, lovely.
Don't stop.

01:47:51.908 --> 01:47:55.810
- Something long and cool, Georg?
- No, thank you, darling.

01:47:56.212 --> 01:47:58.646
- Father?
- Yes, Brigitta?

01:47:59.082 --> 01:48:01.346
Is it true Fräulein Maria
isn't coming back?

01:48:01.651 --> 01:48:04.745
Yes, I suppose it's true.
What have we got here?

01:48:05.054 --> 01:48:09.753
- Pink lemonade.
- Laced with lemonade.

01:48:10.493 --> 01:48:12.017
I don't believe it, Father.

01:48:13.396 --> 01:48:15.421
- What?
- About Fräulein Maria.

01:48:15.832 --> 01:48:17.060
Oh, Fräulein Maria!

01:48:17.367 --> 01:48:20.825
Didn't I tell you what her note said?
I'm sure I did.

01:48:21.571 --> 01:48:24.062
She said she missed her life
at the abbey.

01:48:24.340 --> 01:48:26.501
She had to leave us.

01:48:26.743 --> 01:48:28.335
And that's all there is to it.

01:48:30.046 --> 01:48:32.742
I think I'm brave enough to try
some of that.

01:48:32.949 --> 01:48:35.679
- She didn't even say goodbye.
- She did in her note.

01:48:35.952 --> 01:48:37.749
That isn't the same thing.

01:48:38.054 --> 01:48:39.681
Not too sweet, not too sour.

01:48:40.423 --> 01:48:42.414
Just too pink.

01:48:43.860 --> 01:48:46.954
Father, who is our new governess
going to be?

01:48:53.603 --> 01:48:54.695
Well...

01:48:57.040 --> 01:49:02.273
...you're not going to have
a governess anymore.

01:49:02.612 --> 01:49:05.274
- We're not?
- No.

01:49:07.483 --> 01:49:09.610
You're going to have a new mother.

01:49:10.720 --> 01:49:12.745
A new mother?

01:49:13.590 --> 01:49:16.718
We talked about it last night.
It's all settled.

01:49:16.926 --> 01:49:19.622
And we're all going to be very happy.

01:49:52.629 --> 01:49:55.097
Well, all right, all right.
Run off and play.

01:50:27.063 --> 01:50:28.030
Yes, my children?

01:50:28.231 --> 01:50:30.631
- My name is Liesl.
- Yes, Liesl?

01:50:31.134 --> 01:50:35.070
We, my brothers and sisters,
want to see Fräulein Maria.

01:50:36.239 --> 01:50:38.230
Fräulein Maria?

01:50:39.008 --> 01:50:40.976
Oh, Maria.

01:50:42.879 --> 01:50:44.710
Come in, please.

01:50:48.584 --> 01:50:50.142
Wait here.

01:51:01.097 --> 01:51:04.260
I'm Sister Margaretta. I understand
you inquired about Maria.

01:51:04.534 --> 01:51:07.025
We have to see her.
Will you tell her we're here?

01:51:07.270 --> 01:51:09.864
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- But you've got to!

01:51:10.173 --> 01:51:12.232
- She's our governess.
- We want her back.

01:51:12.442 --> 01:51:14.342
She didn't even say goodbye.

01:51:14.577 --> 01:51:16.340
All we want to do is talk to her.

01:51:17.113 --> 01:51:20.014
I'm very sorry,
but Maria is in seclusion.

01:51:20.249 --> 01:51:23.343
- She hasn't been seeing anyone.
- She'll see us.

01:51:23.586 --> 01:51:26.077
I want to show her my finger.

01:51:26.289 --> 01:51:28.189
Some other time, dear.

01:51:28.458 --> 01:51:29.755
I'll tell her you were here.

01:51:30.026 --> 01:51:33.086
- It was sweet of you to call.
- We have to speak to her!

01:51:33.730 --> 01:51:36.858
Run along, children.
Run along home.

01:51:37.066 --> 01:51:38.693
I'm sure she'd like to see us.

01:51:38.968 --> 01:51:41.232
Sister Margaretta, please.

01:51:41.471 --> 01:51:45.202
- Goodbye, children.
- Sister Margaretta, may we, please?

01:51:47.977 --> 01:51:49.706
What was that about, Sister?

01:51:49.946 --> 01:51:52.141
The von Trapp children,
Reverend Mother.

01:51:52.382 --> 01:51:54.816
They want to see Maria.

01:51:55.084 --> 01:51:57.382
Has she spoken yet?
Has she told you anything?

01:51:57.653 --> 01:52:01.646
She doesn't say a word,
Reverend Mother, except in prayer.

01:52:01.924 --> 01:52:02.913
Poor child.

01:52:03.126 --> 01:52:06.095
It's strange.
She seems happy to be back here...

01:52:06.329 --> 01:52:09.628
...and yet she's unhappy too.

01:52:10.900 --> 01:52:13.960
Perhaps I have been wrong
in leaving her alone so long.

01:52:14.237 --> 01:52:16.933
Bring her to me,
even if she's not yet ready.

01:52:17.140 --> 01:52:18.801
Yes, Reverend Mother.

01:52:24.313 --> 01:52:27.805
Sister Augusta, take our new postulant
to the robing room.

01:52:28.818 --> 01:52:31.082
God bless you, my daughter.

01:52:37.293 --> 01:52:39.022
Yes, bring her in.

01:52:48.037 --> 01:52:50.301
You've been unhappy. I'm sorry.

01:52:52.341 --> 01:52:53.535
Reverend Mother.

01:52:53.876 --> 01:52:56.504
Why did they send you back to us?

01:52:57.346 --> 01:52:59.314
They didn't send me back.
I left.

01:53:01.818 --> 01:53:03.376
Sit down, Maria.

01:53:03.886 --> 01:53:05.683
Tell me what happened.

01:53:10.893 --> 01:53:12.224
I was frightened.

01:53:12.495 --> 01:53:16.955
- Frightened? Were they unkind to you.
- Oh, no!

01:53:17.200 --> 01:53:20.897
No, I was confused. I felt...

01:53:22.371 --> 01:53:24.464
I've never felt that way before.

01:53:24.707 --> 01:53:28.473
I couldn't stay. I knew that here
I'd be away from it. I'd be safe.

01:53:28.711 --> 01:53:33.410
Maria, our abbey is not to be used
as an escape.

01:53:33.683 --> 01:53:35.913
What is it you can't face?

01:53:37.887 --> 01:53:39.320
I can't face him again.

01:53:40.156 --> 01:53:41.680
Him?

01:53:43.259 --> 01:53:45.318
Thank you, Sister Margaretta.

01:53:54.937 --> 01:53:56.564
Captain von Trapp?

01:54:02.011 --> 01:54:04.707
- Are you in love with him?
- I don't know!

01:54:04.947 --> 01:54:06.414
I don't know. I...

01:54:06.949 --> 01:54:10.783
The baroness said I was.
She said that he was in love with me.

01:54:11.053 --> 01:54:13.715
But I didn't want to believe it.

01:54:14.790 --> 01:54:17.088
There were times we looked
at each other.

01:54:17.293 --> 01:54:18.851
I could hardly breathe.

01:54:19.228 --> 01:54:21.924
- Did you let him see your feelings?
- I don't know.

01:54:22.532 --> 01:54:25.194
That's what's torturing me.
I was on God's errand.

01:54:25.401 --> 01:54:30.395
To have asked for his love would have
been wrong. I just couldn't stay.

01:54:32.575 --> 01:54:35.373
I'm ready at this moment
to take my vows.

01:54:36.245 --> 01:54:39.305
- Please help me.
- Maria.

01:54:40.883 --> 01:54:45.582
The love of a man and a woman is holy.
You have a great capacity to love.

01:54:45.821 --> 01:54:48.756
You must find out how God
wants you to spend your love.

01:54:49.058 --> 01:54:52.892
But I pledged my life to God.
I pledged my life to his service.

01:54:53.095 --> 01:54:57.464
My daughter, if you love this man,
it doesn't mean you love God less.

01:54:59.135 --> 01:55:01.000
No.

01:55:01.237 --> 01:55:03.102
You must find out.

01:55:04.840 --> 01:55:07.331
You must go back.

01:55:07.610 --> 01:55:09.578
You can't ask me to do that.

01:55:09.779 --> 01:55:12.270
- Please let me stay. I beg...
- Maria.

01:55:12.481 --> 01:55:16.440
These walls were not built
to shut out problems.

01:55:16.652 --> 01:55:18.244
You have to face them.

01:55:18.821 --> 01:55:22.086
You have to live the life
you were born to live.

01:55:27.964 --> 01:55:32.264
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:32.501 --> 01:55:36.267
<i>Search high and low</i>

01:55:36.505 --> 01:55:41.272
<i>Follow every byway</i>

01:55:41.510 --> 01:55:45.776
<i>Every path you know</i>

01:55:46.215 --> 01:55:50.675
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:50.953 --> 01:55:55.287
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:55:55.524 --> 01:55:59.893
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:00.162 --> 01:56:04.496
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:04.700 --> 01:56:07.794
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:08.037 --> 01:56:12.872
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:13.643 --> 01:56:17.044
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:56:17.313 --> 01:56:23.718
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:56:24.020 --> 01:56:28.320
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:56:28.557 --> 01:56:32.891
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:56:33.162 --> 01:56:37.724
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:37.933 --> 01:56:46.341
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:47.443 --> 01:56:50.935
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:51.247 --> 01:56:56.776
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:57.053 --> 01:57:00.545
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:57:00.790 --> 01:57:07.218
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:57:07.463 --> 01:57:11.900
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:57:12.134 --> 01:57:16.070
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:57:16.739 --> 01:57:21.369
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:57:21.777 --> 01:57:25.873
<i>Till you find...</i>

01:57:26.115 --> 01:57:36.116
<i>...your dream</i>

01:57:38.661 --> 01:57:42.222
Now, it's not like my children
to be secretive.

01:57:42.465 --> 01:57:44.558
We're not being secretive, Father.

01:57:46.235 --> 01:57:49.568
And it's not like my children
to be late for dinner.

01:57:49.839 --> 01:57:53.275
- We lost track of the time.
- I see.

01:57:54.076 --> 01:57:57.477
Who's going to be the first one
to tell me the truth? Friedrich.

01:57:57.747 --> 01:57:59.806
Brigitta. Liesl.

01:58:01.183 --> 01:58:03.413
Where do you think we were, Father?

01:58:09.992 --> 01:58:13.951
If you don't believe us, you must have
some idea of where you think we were.

01:58:17.533 --> 01:58:19.330
- Marta.
- Yes, Father.

01:58:19.535 --> 01:58:20.797
You tell me.

01:58:22.138 --> 01:58:25.767
Friedrich told you, Father.
We were berry picking.

01:58:26.609 --> 01:58:31.273
- I forgot! You were berry picking.
- Yes, we love berry picking.

01:58:31.514 --> 01:58:32.606
All afternoon?

01:58:32.848 --> 01:58:34.577
- We picked thousands.
- Thousands?

01:58:34.784 --> 01:58:37.685
- They were all over the place.
- What kind of berries?

01:58:37.953 --> 01:58:41.218
- Blueberries, sir.
- Blueberries.

01:58:43.159 --> 01:58:46.526
It's too early for blueberries.

01:58:48.030 --> 01:58:50.123
- They were strawberries.
- Strawberries?

01:58:50.833 --> 01:58:53.529
It's been so cold lately,
they turned blue.

01:58:59.375 --> 01:59:01.536
Very well. Show me the berries.

01:59:02.812 --> 01:59:04.006
- We...
- Well...

01:59:04.246 --> 01:59:07.010
- Show me the berries you picked.
- We don't have them.

01:59:07.249 --> 01:59:09.513
You don't have them?
What happened to them?

01:59:09.752 --> 01:59:12.550
- We...
- We ate them.

01:59:12.755 --> 01:59:15.349
- You ate them?
- Yes!

01:59:15.558 --> 01:59:17.150
- They were so good.
- Delicious.

01:59:17.393 --> 01:59:18.587
Very well.

01:59:18.861 --> 01:59:23.992
Since you've obviously stuffed
yourselves on thousands of berries...

01:59:24.233 --> 01:59:28.169
...you can't be hungry anymore,
so I'll have to tell Frau Schmidt...

01:59:28.404 --> 01:59:31.271
...to skip your dinner.

01:59:40.449 --> 01:59:43.247
It's your fault.
We should have told him the truth.

01:59:43.519 --> 01:59:45.487
And made him boiling mad at us?

01:59:45.688 --> 01:59:47.622
It's better than starving to death.

01:59:47.857 --> 01:59:50.724
We didn't do anything wrong.
We just wanted to see her.

01:59:52.027 --> 01:59:55.121
My stomach's making noises.

01:59:55.564 --> 01:59:58.397
The least they could have done
was to let us say hello.

01:59:59.535 --> 02:00:03.437
- I wonder what grass tastes like.
- I feel awful.

02:00:03.873 --> 02:00:08.139
When Fräulein Maria wanted to feel
better she used to sing that song.

02:00:08.744 --> 02:00:10.211
Let's try it.

02:00:10.446 --> 02:00:13.108
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>

02:00:13.415 --> 02:00:17.442
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

02:00:18.287 --> 02:00:20.881
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>

02:00:21.090 --> 02:00:24.150
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

02:00:25.494 --> 02:00:31.455
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

02:00:31.734 --> 02:00:37.730
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:00:37.973 --> 02:00:39.998
Why don't I feel better?

02:00:41.176 --> 02:00:43.474
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>

02:00:43.746 --> 02:00:46.840
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

02:00:47.116 --> 02:00:52.748
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

02:00:53.122 --> 02:00:56.285
- <i>Silver white winters...</i>
- Fräulein Maria's back!

02:00:56.492 --> 02:00:57.789
<i>...that melt into springs</i>

02:00:58.193 --> 02:01:01.458
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:01:01.697 --> 02:01:04.791
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

02:01:05.000 --> 02:01:07.127
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

02:01:07.636 --> 02:01:10.605
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

02:01:10.873 --> 02:01:13.137
<i>And then I don't feel</i>

02:01:13.342 --> 02:01:20.111
<i>So bad</i>

02:01:20.349 --> 02:01:23.375
- Children, I'm so glad to see you.
- We missed you.

02:01:23.619 --> 02:01:24.608
I missed you.

02:01:24.887 --> 02:01:27.014
- Kurt, how are you?
- Hungry.

02:01:28.557 --> 02:01:31.185
- What happened to your finger?
- It got caught.

02:01:31.460 --> 02:01:33.621
- Caught in what?
- Friedrich's teeth.

02:01:34.863 --> 02:01:37.024
- Liesl, you all right?
- Just fair.

02:01:37.232 --> 02:01:40.224
- Any telegrams been delivered lately?
- None at all.

02:01:40.469 --> 02:01:43.905
But I'm learning to accept it.
I'll be glad when school begins.

02:01:44.206 --> 02:01:48.905
Liesl, you can't use school to escape
your problems. You have to face them.

02:01:49.144 --> 02:01:50.577
I have so much to tell you.

02:01:50.846 --> 02:01:52.837
We have things to tell you too.

02:01:53.182 --> 02:01:56.879
The most important thing is
that Father is going to be married.

02:01:57.086 --> 02:01:58.144
Married?

02:01:58.487 --> 02:02:00.512
Yes, to Baroness Schraeder.

02:02:08.430 --> 02:02:09.988
Oh, I see.

02:02:11.834 --> 02:02:15.201
Father, look!
Fräulein Maria's back!

02:02:15.437 --> 02:02:17.496
Fräulein Maria's back from the abbey.

02:02:19.708 --> 02:02:20.766
Good evening, captain.

02:02:22.244 --> 02:02:23.541
Good evening.

02:02:26.081 --> 02:02:27.912
Everyone inside for dinner.

02:02:28.217 --> 02:02:29.775
Dinner!

02:02:39.128 --> 02:02:43.861
You left without saying goodbye.
Even to the children.

02:02:44.867 --> 02:02:46.391
It was wrong of me. Forgive me.

02:02:48.437 --> 02:02:49.597
Why did you?

02:02:49.805 --> 02:02:52.638
Please don't ask me.
The reason no longer exists.

02:02:53.809 --> 02:02:56.903
Fräulein Maria, you've returned.

02:02:58.147 --> 02:02:59.944
Isn't it wonderful, Georg?

02:03:03.252 --> 02:03:05.482
I wish you every happiness,
baroness.

02:03:05.721 --> 02:03:08.417
You too, captain.
The children say you're to marry.

02:03:08.657 --> 02:03:09.783
Thank you, my dear.

02:03:12.327 --> 02:03:15.888
You are back to stay?

02:03:17.966 --> 02:03:21.299
Only until arrangements can be made
for another governess.

02:04:16.992 --> 02:04:18.619
There you are.

02:04:33.008 --> 02:04:35.476
I must speak to cook
about the schnitzel.

02:04:35.744 --> 02:04:39.043
It is entirely too delicious
for my figure.

02:04:39.481 --> 02:04:42.416
And it makes you much too quiet
at the dinner table.

02:04:42.684 --> 02:04:44.675
Or was it the wine?

02:04:44.920 --> 02:04:46.751
Undoubtedly the wine.

02:04:49.324 --> 02:04:51.588
You have no idea
the trouble I'm having...

02:04:51.860 --> 02:04:54.590
...trying to decide on
a wedding present for you.

02:04:54.897 --> 02:04:57.058
Oh, I know. I'm enough.

02:04:57.332 --> 02:05:00.927
But I do want you to have
some little trifle for the occasion.

02:05:01.170 --> 02:05:03.502
At first I thought
of a fountain pen...

02:05:03.739 --> 02:05:06.003
...but you've already got one.

02:05:06.275 --> 02:05:09.210
Then I thought perhaps a villa
in the south of France...

02:05:09.444 --> 02:05:12.106
...but they are so difficult
to gift-wrap.

02:05:12.381 --> 02:05:14.781
Oh, Georg, how do you
feel about yachts?

02:05:15.083 --> 02:05:17.347
A long, sleek one
for the Mediterranean...

02:05:17.586 --> 02:05:20.350
...or a tiny one
for your bathtub, huh?

02:05:22.524 --> 02:05:24.549
- Elsa.
- Where to go on our honeymoon?

02:05:24.793 --> 02:05:26.385
Now, that's a real problem.

02:05:26.595 --> 02:05:29.962
A trip around the world
would be lovely. And then I said:

02:05:30.265 --> 02:05:33.098
"Oh, Elsa, there must be
someplace better to go."

02:05:33.368 --> 02:05:35.802
- But don't worry, darling, I'll...
- Elsa.

02:05:36.471 --> 02:05:37.733
Yes, Georg.

02:05:38.740 --> 02:05:40.071
It's no use...

02:05:41.276 --> 02:05:42.641
...you and I.

02:05:44.213 --> 02:05:47.444
I'm being dishonest to both of us...

02:05:48.784 --> 02:05:50.445
...and utterly unfair to you.

02:05:55.724 --> 02:05:58.454
- When two people talk of marriage...
- No, don't.

02:05:59.328 --> 02:06:01.421
Don't say another word, please.

02:06:04.733 --> 02:06:09.761
You see, there are other things
I've been thinking of.

02:06:10.672 --> 02:06:15.405
Fond as I am of you, I really don't
think you're the right man for me.

02:06:17.946 --> 02:06:20.437
You're much too independent.

02:06:20.749 --> 02:06:25.448
And I need someone
who needs me desperately...

02:06:25.754 --> 02:06:28.746
...or at least needs
my money desperately.

02:06:30.926 --> 02:06:35.829
I've enjoyed every moment we've had
together and I do thank you for that.

02:06:38.600 --> 02:06:40.500
Now, if you'll forgive me...

02:06:40.702 --> 02:06:42.761
...I'll go inside,
pack my little bags...

02:06:43.005 --> 02:06:45.496
...and return to Vienna
where I belong.

02:06:50.879 --> 02:06:52.710
And somewhere out there...

02:06:53.015 --> 02:06:57.384
...is a young lady who, I think...

02:06:57.653 --> 02:06:58.881
...will never be a nun.

02:07:11.033 --> 02:07:13.365
Auf Wiedersehen, darling.

02:07:39.094 --> 02:07:40.254
Hello.

02:07:46.068 --> 02:07:49.663
I thought I just might find you here.

02:07:53.842 --> 02:07:56.106
Was there something you wanted?

02:07:56.545 --> 02:07:59.673
No, no, no. Sit down, please.

02:08:00.615 --> 02:08:01.946
Please.

02:08:07.089 --> 02:08:08.420
May I?

02:08:20.802 --> 02:08:25.535
You know, I was thinking
and I was wondering two things:

02:08:26.708 --> 02:08:30.940
Why did you run away to the abbey?

02:08:31.780 --> 02:08:36.444
And what was it
that made you come back?

02:08:38.120 --> 02:08:42.580
Well, I had an obligation
to fulfill...

02:08:42.791 --> 02:08:44.918
...and I came back to fulfill it.

02:08:45.560 --> 02:08:46.993
Is that all?

02:08:48.330 --> 02:08:50.491
And I missed the children.

02:08:50.832 --> 02:08:51.992
Yes.

02:08:53.268 --> 02:08:56.169
- Only the children?
- No. Yes.

02:08:56.405 --> 02:09:00.239
- Isn't it right that I missed them?
- Oh, yes. Yes, of course.

02:09:00.442 --> 02:09:03.070
I was only hoping that perhaps you...

02:09:04.179 --> 02:09:05.942
Perhaps you might...

02:09:07.682 --> 02:09:08.910
Yes?

02:09:10.685 --> 02:09:15.987
Well, nothing was the same
when you were away...

02:09:16.758 --> 02:09:19.989
...and it'll be all wrong again
after you leave...

02:09:20.195 --> 02:09:24.859
...and I just thought perhaps
you might change your mind.

02:09:28.937 --> 02:09:33.169
Well, I'm sure the baroness will be
able to make things fine for you.

02:09:33.442 --> 02:09:34.773
Maria...

02:09:36.878 --> 02:09:40.370
- There isn't going to be any baroness.
- There isn't?

02:09:42.784 --> 02:09:44.149
No.

02:09:44.453 --> 02:09:46.216
I don't understand.

02:09:48.623 --> 02:09:52.719
Well, we've called off our engagement,
you see, and...

02:09:52.994 --> 02:09:56.452
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Yes. You are?

02:09:57.632 --> 02:09:59.725
- You did?
- Yes.

02:10:00.869 --> 02:10:05.397
Well, you can't marry someone
when you're...

02:10:07.976 --> 02:10:10.035
...in love with someone else...

02:10:13.415 --> 02:10:14.848
...can you?

02:10:49.718 --> 02:10:52.016
The Reverend Mother always says:

02:10:52.254 --> 02:10:55.690
"When the Lord closes a door,
somewhere He opens a window."

02:11:04.099 --> 02:11:07.125
What else does
the Reverend Mother say?

02:11:08.069 --> 02:11:10.469
That you have to look for your life.

02:11:12.140 --> 02:11:14.700
Is that why you came back?

02:11:18.747 --> 02:11:20.214
And have you found it...

02:11:21.216 --> 02:11:22.376
...Maria?

02:11:24.152 --> 02:11:26.143
I think I have.

02:11:28.890 --> 02:11:30.289
I know I have.

02:11:32.794 --> 02:11:34.455
I love you.

02:11:38.433 --> 02:11:40.298
Oh, can this be happening to me?

02:11:43.672 --> 02:11:49.076
<i>Perhaps I had a wicked childhood</i>

02:11:50.579 --> 02:11:55.812
<i>Perhaps I had a miserable youth</i>

02:11:57.686 --> 02:12:03.625
<i>But somewhere</i>
<i>In my wicked, miserable past</i>

02:12:04.125 --> 02:12:09.927
<i>There must have been a moment of truth</i>

02:12:10.865 --> 02:12:17.634
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:12:18.373 --> 02:12:24.369
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:12:25.013 --> 02:12:31.816
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:12:32.687 --> 02:12:40.321
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:12:41.563 --> 02:12:44.532
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:12:45.667 --> 02:12:49.535
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:12:50.372 --> 02:12:59.246
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:00.815 --> 02:13:10.315
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:13:11.192 --> 02:13:16.027
Do you know when I first
started loving you?

02:13:16.431 --> 02:13:20.333
That night at dinner, when you sat
on that ridiculous pine cone.

02:13:20.568 --> 02:13:21.865
What?

02:13:23.204 --> 02:13:26.662
I knew the first time you blew
that silly whistle.

02:13:27.575 --> 02:13:29.566
Oh, my love.

02:13:33.348 --> 02:13:41.255
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:13:43.224 --> 02:13:49.060
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:13:50.432 --> 02:13:57.463
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:58.273 --> 02:14:05.975
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:14:07.148 --> 02:14:10.640
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:14:11.386 --> 02:14:14.412
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:14:14.656 --> 02:14:20.458
<i>So somewhere in my youth...</i>

02:14:20.729 --> 02:14:22.959
<i>...or childhood</i>

02:14:26.067 --> 02:14:32.597
<i>I must have done something</i>

02:14:34.642 --> 02:14:47.282
<i>Something good</i>

02:14:53.995 --> 02:14:55.519
Maria.

02:14:57.365 --> 02:15:01.961
Is there anyone I should go to,
to ask permission to marry you?

02:15:05.874 --> 02:15:08.434
- Why don't we ask...
- The children?

02:16:56.951 --> 02:17:00.978
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:01.789 --> 02:17:05.486
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

02:17:06.461 --> 02:17:10.625
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

02:17:11.065 --> 02:17:12.054
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

02:17:12.300 --> 02:17:15.565
<i>A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>A clown</i>

02:17:15.770 --> 02:17:20.332
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

02:17:20.775 --> 02:17:24.802
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

02:17:25.513 --> 02:17:29.813
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

02:17:30.184 --> 02:17:34.120
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

02:17:34.455 --> 02:17:39.449
<i>Oh, how do you solve</i>
<i>A problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:39.827 --> 02:17:46.460
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam</i>
<i>In your hand?</i>

02:19:52.560 --> 02:19:54.118
Herr Detweiler!

02:19:56.731 --> 02:19:59.393
- Heil Hitler.
- Oh, good afternoon, Herr Zeller.

02:19:59.634 --> 02:20:02.933
Perhaps you've not heard.
I am now the Gauleiter.

02:20:03.237 --> 02:20:04.761
Heil Hitler.

02:20:05.673 --> 02:20:06.833
Heil Hitler.

02:20:07.141 --> 02:20:09.405
I've come from
Captain von Trapp's house.

02:20:09.844 --> 02:20:13.439
The only one in the area
not flying the Third Reich flag...

02:20:13.681 --> 02:20:14.943
...since the Anschluss.

02:20:15.149 --> 02:20:17.310
- But we have dealt with that.
- I don't...

02:20:17.585 --> 02:20:20.520
The housekeeper told me
that I would find you here.

02:20:20.788 --> 02:20:22.483
The only thing she'd tell me.

02:20:22.990 --> 02:20:25.515
What kind of information
are you looking for?

02:20:25.793 --> 02:20:27.658
When will the captain return?

02:20:28.196 --> 02:20:32.132
Well, he's on his honeymoon trip.
He's not been in touch with us.

02:20:32.366 --> 02:20:37.201
Am I to believe he hasn't communicated
with his children in over a month?

02:20:37.472 --> 02:20:39.372
How many men do you know...

02:20:39.640 --> 02:20:42.939
...who communicate with their children
while honeymooning?

02:20:43.845 --> 02:20:47.542
Upon his return, he'll fill
his proper position in the new order.

02:20:47.849 --> 02:20:50.215
Naturally.
And may I congratulate you...

02:20:50.451 --> 02:20:55.115
...and your people in allowing the
festival to go on tonight as planned.

02:20:55.656 --> 02:20:59.114
Why should it not go on?
Nothing in Austria has changed.

02:20:59.360 --> 02:21:02.761
Singing and music will
show this to the world.

02:21:02.964 --> 02:21:04.659
Austria is the same.

02:21:05.533 --> 02:21:06.898
Heil Hitler.

02:21:09.070 --> 02:21:10.662
Heil Hitler.

02:21:12.340 --> 02:21:13.568
Come, let's go home.

02:21:13.808 --> 02:21:17.300
- Why was he so cross?
- Everybody's cross these days.

02:21:17.512 --> 02:21:20.879
Maybe the flag with the black spider
makes people nervous.

02:21:21.082 --> 02:21:24.017
- Will Father be in trouble?
- He doesn't have to be.

02:21:24.252 --> 02:21:26.982
The thing to do
is to get along with everybody.

02:21:27.221 --> 02:21:29.416
Remember that tonight at the concert.

02:21:29.657 --> 02:21:32.558
Are we really going to sing
before a lot of people?

02:21:32.760 --> 02:21:34.853
Look. The von Trapp Family Singers:

02:21:35.062 --> 02:21:39.658
Liesl, Friedrich, Louisa, Brigitta,
Kurt, Marta and Gretl.

02:21:39.867 --> 02:21:44.236
- Why am I always last?
- Because you are the most important.

02:21:44.939 --> 02:21:46.566
There we go.

02:21:52.446 --> 02:21:55.904
Are you sure Father will approve
of our singing in public?

02:21:56.117 --> 02:21:58.415
He'll be pleased and proud.

02:21:58.886 --> 02:22:01.354
- Liesl, do you think so?
- Don't you trust me?

02:22:01.556 --> 02:22:02.580
No.

02:22:02.790 --> 02:22:04.883
You're a very intelligent girl.

02:22:05.426 --> 02:22:07.587
Liesl. Liesl!

02:22:08.529 --> 02:22:09.723
Rolfe!

02:22:10.731 --> 02:22:12.756
I'm so glad to see you.
It's been su...

02:22:12.967 --> 02:22:14.059
Good afternoon.

02:22:14.468 --> 02:22:17.403
Give this to your father
as soon as he's home.

02:22:18.072 --> 02:22:19.937
- He's on his honeymoon.
- I know.

02:22:20.141 --> 02:22:23.474
- You do?
- We make it our business to know all.

02:22:24.212 --> 02:22:26.772
- Who's "we"?
- See that he gets it.

02:22:26.981 --> 02:22:29.313
- What is it?
- It's a telegram from Berlin.

02:22:30.151 --> 02:22:32.642
Don't you want to deliver it yourself?

02:22:33.120 --> 02:22:35.748
I'm occupied
with more important matters.

02:22:35.957 --> 02:22:38.448
And your father had better be too.

02:22:38.726 --> 02:22:40.216
But, Rolfe!

02:23:03.317 --> 02:23:04.978
Father!

02:23:05.253 --> 02:23:07.915
- We didn't expect you so soon.
- Hello, hello!

02:23:08.155 --> 02:23:10.953
We didn't expect you home
until next week!

02:23:11.158 --> 02:23:16.596
- Did you bring souvenirs from Paris?
- Hello! How are you?

02:23:17.698 --> 02:23:18.995
Why didn't you call us?

02:23:19.200 --> 02:23:21.134
We couldn't get through.

02:23:21.435 --> 02:23:23.369
I had nothing to do with that.

02:23:23.638 --> 02:23:25.663
We came back as fast as we could.

02:23:25.973 --> 02:23:28.134
Well, well, well! We missed you!

02:23:28.376 --> 02:23:30.810
- We missed you!
- We missed kissing you.

02:23:31.012 --> 02:23:33.845
We missed all the noise
in the morning.

02:23:34.115 --> 02:23:38.313
- Mostly, we missed hearing you sing.
- Oh, you came back just in time.

02:23:38.519 --> 02:23:40.282
Look, Fräulein Maria...

02:23:40.488 --> 02:23:42.115
I mean Mother.

02:23:42.523 --> 02:23:45.014
We're going to sing
in the festival tonight.

02:23:45.226 --> 02:23:47.353
We've been having a lovely time!

02:23:47.628 --> 02:23:49.687
We've been rehearsing all...

02:23:51.198 --> 02:23:53.530
Surprise! Surprise!

02:23:54.201 --> 02:23:56.692
Surprises for you on the terrace.

02:23:59.740 --> 02:24:01.139
We'll talk about this.

02:24:01.342 --> 02:24:05.642
I would've told you but you were away.
I had to make a last-minute decision.

02:24:05.913 --> 02:24:08.404
I was fortunate to enter them at all.

02:24:08.649 --> 02:24:13.382
They'll be the talk of the festival.
Imagine, seven children in one family!

02:24:13.587 --> 02:24:15.214
Max!

02:24:15.823 --> 02:24:18.656
Somehow I recall having made it
quite clear to you...

02:24:18.926 --> 02:24:21.588
...how I feel about my family
singing in public!

02:24:21.862 --> 02:24:23.557
The committee was enchanted.

02:24:23.764 --> 02:24:26.927
- What did they say?
- I have never heard such enthusiasm.

02:24:27.201 --> 02:24:31.501
- Don't you think just this once...?
- Absolutely out of the question.

02:24:31.739 --> 02:24:35.869
- Georg, this is for Austria.
- For Austria?

02:24:36.243 --> 02:24:39.508
- There is no Austria!
- But the Anschluss was peaceful.

02:24:39.747 --> 02:24:43.205
- Let's at least be grateful for that.
- Grateful?

02:24:45.086 --> 02:24:46.747
You know, Max...

02:24:47.621 --> 02:24:50.886
...sometimes I don't believe
I know you.

02:24:53.561 --> 02:24:54.926
Father, I forgot.

02:24:55.763 --> 02:24:57.355
This is for you.

02:25:07.141 --> 02:25:11.134
Maria, he has got to at least pretend
to work with these people.

02:25:11.412 --> 02:25:12.936
You must convince him.

02:25:13.147 --> 02:25:15.911
Max, I can't ask him
to be less than he is.

02:25:16.150 --> 02:25:19.449
Then I'll talk to him.
If the children don't sing, well...

02:25:19.720 --> 02:25:21.950
...it will be a reflection
on Austria.

02:25:22.757 --> 02:25:26.124
Oh, I know.
It wouldn't do me any good either.

02:25:31.298 --> 02:25:33.960
Mother? That sounds so nice.

02:25:34.235 --> 02:25:36.965
- I like calling you "Mother."
- I like hearing it.

02:25:37.171 --> 02:25:40.902
You love Father very much.
I can tell you do.

02:25:41.108 --> 02:25:41.904
Very much.

02:25:42.176 --> 02:25:45.475
Mother, what do you do when you
think you love someone?

02:25:46.180 --> 02:25:51.482
I mean, when you stop loving someone
or he stops loving you?

02:25:54.088 --> 02:25:56.147
Well, you cry a little.

02:25:56.590 --> 02:25:58.683
Then you wait for the sun to come out.

02:25:58.993 --> 02:26:00.324
It always does.

02:26:00.594 --> 02:26:04.155
There are so many things I think
I should know but I don't.

02:26:04.365 --> 02:26:06.333
- I really don't.
- How can you?

02:26:06.600 --> 02:26:08.795
Sometimes I feel the world is ending.

02:26:09.036 --> 02:26:12.267
- Then you feel it's just beginning?
- Yes!

02:26:12.473 --> 02:26:16.705
It was that way with me. And for you
it will be just as wonderful.

02:26:17.378 --> 02:26:19.278
Do you really think so?

02:26:20.181 --> 02:26:24.117
<i>When you're 16 going on 17</i>

02:26:24.385 --> 02:26:27.980
<i>Waiting for life to start</i>

02:26:28.656 --> 02:26:32.490
<i>Somebody kind</i>
<i>Who touches your mind</i>

02:26:32.726 --> 02:26:37.026
<i>Will suddenly touch your heart</i>

02:26:37.465 --> 02:26:39.160
<i>When that happens</i>

02:26:39.633 --> 02:26:41.567
<i>After it happens</i>

02:26:41.802 --> 02:26:45.670
<i>Nothing is quite the same</i>

02:26:45.906 --> 02:26:47.464
<i>Somehow I know</i>

02:26:47.741 --> 02:26:49.868
<i>I'll jump up and go</i>

02:26:50.077 --> 02:26:54.377
<i>If ever he calls my name</i>

02:26:54.648 --> 02:26:58.550
<i>Gone are your old ideas of life</i>

02:26:58.819 --> 02:27:03.017
<i>The old ideas grow dim</i>

02:27:03.257 --> 02:27:07.660
<i>Lo and behold</i>
<i>You're someone's wife</i>

02:27:08.596 --> 02:27:14.592
<i>And you belong to him</i>

02:27:14.902 --> 02:27:19.202
<i>You may think this kind of adventure</i>

02:27:19.406 --> 02:27:23.274
<i>Never may come to you</i>

02:27:24.378 --> 02:27:29.748
<i>Darling, 16 going on 17</i>

02:27:30.584 --> 02:27:34.714
<i>Wait a year...</i>

02:27:35.523 --> 02:27:40.756
<i>- I'll wait a year</i>
<i>...or two</i>

02:27:41.195 --> 02:27:48.533
<i>Just wait a year...</i>

02:27:49.403 --> 02:27:58.038
<i>...or two</i>

02:28:00.447 --> 02:28:02.039
Liesl.

02:28:18.499 --> 02:28:19.830
What is it?

02:28:20.768 --> 02:28:22.133
Berlin.

02:28:22.603 --> 02:28:24.468
They've offered me a commission.

02:28:24.738 --> 02:28:27.263
I've been requested
to accept immediately...

02:28:27.508 --> 02:28:31.501
...and report to their naval base
at Bremerhaven tomorrow.

02:28:32.112 --> 02:28:36.105
I knew this would happen.
I didn't think it would be so soon.

02:28:36.350 --> 02:28:39.842
To refuse them would be fatal
for all of us.

02:28:41.088 --> 02:28:44.854
And joining them would be unthinkable.

02:28:51.031 --> 02:28:52.794
Get the children all together.

02:28:53.133 --> 02:28:56.330
Don't say anything to worry them.
Just get them ready.

02:28:57.304 --> 02:28:59.670
We've got to get out of Austria...

02:29:01.342 --> 02:29:03.003
...and this house...

02:29:05.346 --> 02:29:06.779
...tonight.

02:29:50.691 --> 02:29:53.091
This strains my back
and breaks my heart...

02:29:53.360 --> 02:29:56.193
...when I think of the children
missing the festival.

02:29:56.497 --> 02:29:59.159
By your announcement
we'll be over the border.

02:29:59.400 --> 02:30:01.834
Do you appreciate
the sacrifice I'm making?

02:30:02.036 --> 02:30:03.333
You have no choice.

02:30:03.570 --> 02:30:06.403
I know. That's why I'm making it.

02:30:07.107 --> 02:30:09.234
Why doesn't Father turn the motor on?

02:30:09.443 --> 02:30:12.879
Because he doesn't want anyone
to hear us.

02:30:16.517 --> 02:30:18.951
What will Frau Schmidt and Franz say?

02:30:19.219 --> 02:30:22.746
They'll be able to answer honestly
they didn't know anything.

02:30:22.956 --> 02:30:27.188
- Will we be coming back here?
- Someday, Liesl. I do hope someday.

02:30:27.428 --> 02:30:32.365
Are Father and Uncle Max going to push
the car all the way to Switzerland?

02:30:59.159 --> 02:31:01.559
Something wrong
with your car, captain?

02:31:01.895 --> 02:31:04.159
Yes, we couldn't get it started.

02:31:07.935 --> 02:31:09.163
Karl.

02:31:11.138 --> 02:31:14.630
Fix Captain von Trapp's car
so that it will start.

02:31:37.831 --> 02:31:39.628
Excellent, Karl.

02:31:43.003 --> 02:31:46.166
I've not asked you where you
and your family are going.

02:31:46.673 --> 02:31:48.800
Nor have you asked me why I'm here.

02:31:49.009 --> 02:31:52.775
Apparently we both suffer
from a deplorable lack of curiosity.

02:31:53.647 --> 02:31:56.115
You never answered the telegram...

02:31:56.350 --> 02:31:59.649
...from the Admiral of the Navy
of the Third Reich.

02:31:59.887 --> 02:32:02.355
I was under the impression,
Herr Zeller...

02:32:02.623 --> 02:32:06.115
...that the contents of telegrams
in Austria are private!

02:32:06.827 --> 02:32:10.354
At least, the Austria I know.

02:32:11.498 --> 02:32:13.125
I have my orders...

02:32:13.367 --> 02:32:15.528
...to take you
to Bremerhaven tonight...

02:32:15.803 --> 02:32:17.998
...where you will accept
your commission.

02:32:19.139 --> 02:32:24.577
I'm afraid that's going to be
quite impossible.

02:32:25.179 --> 02:32:26.908
You see, we...

02:32:27.481 --> 02:32:30.314
...all of us, the entire family,
will be...

02:32:31.385 --> 02:32:33.410
...singing in the festival tonight.

02:32:33.720 --> 02:32:36.188
As a matter of fact, we're going now.

02:32:36.824 --> 02:32:39.691
We couldn't possibly
let them down now.

02:32:39.893 --> 02:32:42.862
- I just hope we're not too late.
- Yes.

02:32:43.096 --> 02:32:45.997
You ask me to believe that you,
Captain von Trapp...

02:32:46.233 --> 02:32:47.700
...are singing in a concert?

02:32:48.101 --> 02:32:52.231
Believe me, it will be a performance
beyond anything even I've dreamt of.

02:32:52.606 --> 02:32:57.236
Like you, Herr Zeller,
I, too, am a man of hidden talents.

02:32:57.945 --> 02:32:59.276
Yes.

02:32:59.546 --> 02:33:02.037
Here, program.

02:33:07.054 --> 02:33:09.386
It says only the names
of the children.

02:33:09.623 --> 02:33:12.888
It says
the von Trapp Family Singers...

02:33:13.126 --> 02:33:16.186
...and I am the head of
the von Trapp family, am I not?

02:33:18.465 --> 02:33:22.265
And these travel clothes
that you're all wearing?

02:33:23.103 --> 02:33:24.627
Our costumes, naturally.

02:33:24.905 --> 02:33:28.306
This night air is not good
for the children's voices.

02:33:34.548 --> 02:33:38.075
Well, a slight delay in my orders
will not be serious.

02:33:39.286 --> 02:33:40.810
Therefore...

02:33:41.655 --> 02:33:43.282
...you will sing.

02:33:44.224 --> 02:33:46.215
You will all sing.

02:33:46.593 --> 02:33:49.118
But only because that's what I want.

02:33:50.063 --> 02:33:53.499
It will demonstrate that nothing
in Austria has changed.

02:33:54.234 --> 02:33:56.429
And when you have finished singing...

02:33:56.737 --> 02:33:59.900
...you, Captain von Trapp, will be
taken to Bremerhaven.

02:34:01.174 --> 02:34:03.904
Now, if you will all get
into your car...

02:34:04.144 --> 02:34:07.978
...we will escort the von Trapp Family
Singers to the festival.

02:34:08.849 --> 02:34:11.010
No escort will be necessary.

02:34:11.251 --> 02:34:13.742
Necessary? A pleasure, captain.

02:34:14.655 --> 02:34:18.523
After all, we would not want you
to get lost in the crowds.

02:34:19.760 --> 02:34:21.250
Would we?

02:34:21.929 --> 02:34:23.089
No.

02:34:39.313 --> 02:34:42.476
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

02:34:42.683 --> 02:34:45.880
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

02:34:46.153 --> 02:34:49.611
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

02:34:49.823 --> 02:34:53.623
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

02:35:03.203 --> 02:35:05.364
<i>Tea with jam</i>
<i>Jam and bread</i>

02:35:11.244 --> 02:35:14.577
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- A, B, C</i>

02:35:14.815 --> 02:35:18.046
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- Do-re-mi</i>

02:35:18.251 --> 02:35:21.846
<i>Tea with jam and bread</i>

02:35:22.089 --> 02:35:23.420
<i>With jam and bread</i>

02:35:23.690 --> 02:35:25.214
<i>With jam</i>
<i>With jam...</i>

02:35:25.425 --> 02:35:34.231
<i>...and bread</i>

02:35:56.223 --> 02:35:59.351
My fellow Austrians...

02:36:00.627 --> 02:36:05.189
...I shall not be seeing you again,
perhaps for a very long time.

02:36:06.600 --> 02:36:08.261
I would like to sing for you now...

02:36:09.870 --> 02:36:11.428
...a love song.

02:36:13.407 --> 02:36:15.602
I know you share this love.

02:36:16.910 --> 02:36:20.607
I pray that you will never let it die.

02:36:33.393 --> 02:36:36.920
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:37.130 --> 02:36:40.327
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:40.600 --> 02:36:46.334
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

02:36:46.740 --> 02:36:49.800
<i>Small and white</i>

02:36:50.077 --> 02:36:52.841
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:36:53.413 --> 02:36:58.510
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:36:59.286 --> 02:37:01.311
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:01.588 --> 02:37:05.183
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:05.425 --> 02:37:11.091
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:37:12.599 --> 02:37:15.090
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:15.335 --> 02:37:17.963
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:18.171 --> 02:37:24.167
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:37:28.682 --> 02:37:31.776
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:32.018 --> 02:37:33.349
<i>Edel...</i>

02:37:40.727 --> 02:37:43.821
<i>Small and white</i>

02:37:44.030 --> 02:37:46.897
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:37:47.134 --> 02:37:52.470
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:53.306 --> 02:37:55.274
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:55.475 --> 02:37:58.876
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:59.546 --> 02:38:05.542
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:38:06.019 --> 02:38:08.920
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:09.222 --> 02:38:11.986
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:12.592 --> 02:38:20.829
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:38:38.552 --> 02:38:40.110
I think it'll work.

02:38:40.854 --> 02:38:42.617
I shall miss all of you.

02:38:43.123 --> 02:38:45.557
I shall miss the money
I could have made with you.

02:38:48.962 --> 02:38:50.520
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

02:38:51.264 --> 02:38:53.926
The competition has come
to its conclusion...

02:38:54.201 --> 02:38:57.295
...except, we don't know
yet what that conclusion will be.

02:38:58.271 --> 02:39:00.796
And while the judges
arrive at their decision...

02:39:01.074 --> 02:39:04.100
...I have been given permission
to offer you an encore.

02:39:04.377 --> 02:39:07.574
This will be the last opportunity
the von Trapps will have...

02:39:07.814 --> 02:39:10.214
...of singing together
for a long, long time.

02:39:11.284 --> 02:39:15.277
Even now, officials are waiting
in this auditorium...

02:39:15.555 --> 02:39:18.285
...to escort Captain von Trapp
to his new command...

02:39:18.491 --> 02:39:22.052
...in the naval forces
of the Third Reich.

02:39:26.733 --> 02:39:31.261
And so, ladies and gentlemen,
the family von Trapp again...

02:39:31.905 --> 02:39:34.169
...to bid you farewell.

02:39:41.414 --> 02:39:45.009
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

02:39:45.285 --> 02:39:48.618
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

02:39:49.122 --> 02:39:52.990
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

02:39:53.193 --> 02:39:55.627
<i>Is popping out to say "coo-coo"</i>

02:39:55.829 --> 02:39:57.490
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:57.764 --> 02:39:58.753
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:59.032 --> 02:40:00.624
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

02:40:00.834 --> 02:40:02.631
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

02:40:02.869 --> 02:40:05.633
<i>To say goodbye</i>

02:40:05.839 --> 02:40:11.004
<i>To you</i>

02:40:13.980 --> 02:40:17.507
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

02:40:17.784 --> 02:40:21.515
<i>We hate to go</i>
<i>And miss this pretty sight</i>

02:40:27.694 --> 02:40:31.289
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

02:40:31.498 --> 02:40:35.161
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

02:40:41.474 --> 02:40:45.069
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:45.312 --> 02:40:46.904
<i>We flit, we float</i>

02:40:47.180 --> 02:40:48.841
<i>We fleetly flee, we fly</i>

02:40:55.221 --> 02:40:59.021
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:59.225 --> 02:41:02.592
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>
<i>And so must I</i>

02:41:02.862 --> 02:41:06.662
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:06.900 --> 02:41:12.600
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:12.839 --> 02:41:18.038
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:18.278 --> 02:41:25.446
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:57.250 --> 02:42:01.380
Ladies and gentlemen, I have here the
decision of our distinguished judges.

02:42:01.588 --> 02:42:04.148
We will start with the award
for third prize.

02:42:04.791 --> 02:42:07.123
For this honor,
the judges have named...

02:42:07.394 --> 02:42:11.990
...the first soloist of the choir
of St. Agatha's Church in Murback.

02:42:12.265 --> 02:42:14.495
Fräulein Schweiger.

02:42:51.438 --> 02:42:55.374
Second prize
to The Toby Reiser Quintet.

02:43:23.336 --> 02:43:27.500
And the first prize,
the highest honor in all Austria...

02:43:27.740 --> 02:43:30.834
...the von Trapp Family Singers.

02:43:43.223 --> 02:43:44.884
The family von Trapp.

02:43:59.506 --> 02:44:00.564
They're gone!

02:44:19.259 --> 02:44:20.692
Come with me.

02:44:24.531 --> 02:44:26.522
Quickly, quickly.

02:44:27.433 --> 02:44:29.628
I have a place you can hide.

02:44:30.370 --> 02:44:33.635
Slowly, slowly.

02:44:44.617 --> 02:44:46.312
Open this gate.

02:44:47.453 --> 02:44:49.045
Good evening.

02:44:51.558 --> 02:44:52.991
Hurry up, woman.

02:45:12.845 --> 02:45:14.107
Two men in there.

02:45:14.314 --> 02:45:16.179
Six of you cover the yard.

02:45:16.416 --> 02:45:18.646
You two, cover the corridor.

02:45:33.132 --> 02:45:36.693
Reverend Mother, we didn't realize
we put the abbey in this danger.

02:45:36.970 --> 02:45:39.495
No, Maria, it was right for you
to come here.

02:45:39.706 --> 02:45:41.606
We thought we might borrow
your car.

02:45:41.808 --> 02:45:43.708
I'm afraid our car will do you
no good now.

02:45:44.310 --> 02:45:45.971
I've been listening to the wires.

02:45:46.179 --> 02:45:48.704
The borders have just been closed.

02:45:54.554 --> 02:45:56.852
All right,
if the borders are closed...

02:45:58.157 --> 02:46:01.456
...then we'll drive up into the hills
and go over the mountains on foot.

02:46:02.061 --> 02:46:04.052
- The children...
- We'll help them.

02:46:04.330 --> 02:46:06.491
We can do it without help, Father.

02:46:07.533 --> 02:46:08.898
Maria.

02:46:09.636 --> 02:46:12.230
You will not be alone.
Remember:

02:46:12.472 --> 02:46:15.566
"I will lift up mine eyes unto
the hills from whence cometh my help."

02:46:16.542 --> 02:46:17.634
Yes, Mother.

02:46:19.012 --> 02:46:21.173
- I'm scared.
- Me too.

02:46:33.259 --> 02:46:34.419
God be with you.

02:46:41.367 --> 02:46:42.925
- Mother.
- Yes?

02:46:43.169 --> 02:46:46.366
Would it help if we sang
about our favorite things?

02:46:46.606 --> 02:46:49.598
No, darling.
This is one time it would not help.

02:46:49.876 --> 02:46:53.073
You must be very quiet.
Hold tight to me.

02:49:07.747 --> 02:49:08.975
Let's try the roof.

02:50:05.238 --> 02:50:07.468
Rolfe, please.

02:50:12.578 --> 02:50:14.068
No, wait.

02:50:23.890 --> 02:50:25.221
Maria.

02:50:26.292 --> 02:50:27.725
Children.

02:50:31.764 --> 02:50:34.790
It's you we want, not them.

02:50:35.167 --> 02:50:36.896
Put that down.

02:50:37.970 --> 02:50:41.269
Not another move,
or I'll shoot.

02:50:42.975 --> 02:50:45.000
You're only a boy.

02:50:48.014 --> 02:50:51.677
- You don't really belong to them.
- Stay where you are.

02:50:53.452 --> 02:50:55.443
Come away with us.

02:50:56.689 --> 02:50:57.849
Before it's too late.

02:50:58.457 --> 02:51:00.789
Not another step.
I'll kill you.

02:51:03.095 --> 02:51:06.428
- You give that to me, Rolfe.
- Did you hear me?

02:51:07.433 --> 02:51:08.991
I'll kill you.

02:51:10.870 --> 02:51:12.337
Rolfe.

02:51:30.723 --> 02:51:32.054
You'll never be one of them.

02:51:34.827 --> 02:51:36.522
Lieutenant!

02:51:36.796 --> 02:51:37.922
They're here!

02:51:38.130 --> 02:51:39.688
They're here, lieutenant!

02:52:21.007 --> 02:52:22.668
Reverend Mother.

02:52:23.943 --> 02:52:25.774
I have sinned.

02:52:26.946 --> 02:52:29.107
I too, Reverend Mother.

02:52:30.750 --> 02:52:33.082
What is this sin, my children?

02:53:38.365 --> 02:54:08.354
